$$h=\dfrac{\frac{\pi}{2}-\frac{\pi}{6}}{2}=\dfrac{\pi}{6}$$
and the function values are needed at $x=\dfrac{\pi}{6},\ \dfrac{\pi}{3},\ \dfrac{\pi}{2}$, where $f(x)=\dfrac{1+\cos x}{\sin x}$:

\extable{Ts25_1}

By the trapezoidal rule,
$$\int_a^b f(x)\,dx\approx\dfrac{h}{2}\left\{f(x_0)+2f(x_1)+f(x_2)\right\}$$
with $\dfrac{h}{2}=\dfrac{\pi}{12}$:
$$\begin{aligned}\int_{\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}\dfrac{1+\cos x}{\sin x}\,dx&\approx\dfrac{\pi}{12}\left\{(2+\sqrt{3})+2\sqrt{3}+1\right\}\\ &=\dfrac{\pi}{12}(3+3\sqrt{3})\\ &=\dfrac{\pi}{4}(1+\sqrt{3})\end{aligned}$$','3: Substitutes h and the 3 exact function values into the formula then gives simplest exact result; 2: Substantial progress eg. correct procedure but with one error, or result not exact and simplified; 1: Some progress eg. at least 2 exact function values found',1308,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Substantial progress, e.g. correct procedure but with one error, or result not exact and simplified"], [1, "Some progress, e.g. at least 2 exact function values found"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Substitutes $h$ and the 3 exact function values into the formula then gives simplest exact result", "source_original": {"latex": "$h=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$, $f(x)=\\dfrac{1+\\cos x}{\\sin x}$\n\n\\extable{Ts25_1}\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\dfrac{1+\\cos}{\\sin x}\\,dx&\\approx\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\left\\{(2+\\sqrt{3})+2\\sqrt{3}+1\\right\\}\\\\ &=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}(1+\\sqrt{3})\\end{aligned}$$", "criteria": [[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Substantial progress, e.g. correct procedure but with one error, or result not exact and simplified"], [1, "Some progress, e.g. at least 2 exact function values found"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: integrand was missing the $x$ after $\\cos$.", "explained": "Working explained: how h is found, which x values, the trapezoidal formula (owner request, 11 Nov)."}');
