$$\begin{aligned}\dfrac{f''(x)}{f(x)}&=\dfrac{1-\ln x}{x^2}\times\dfrac{x}{\ln x}\\ &=\dfrac{1-\ln x}{x\ln x}\end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned}\therefore\ \int_e^{e^2}\dfrac{1-\ln x}{x\ln x}\,dx&=\left[\ln\left(\dfrac{\ln x}{x}\right)\right]_e^{e^2}\\ &=\left[\ln(\ln x)-\ln x\right]_e^{e^2}\\ &=\ln 2-\ln 1-(2-1)\\ &=\ln 2-1\end{aligned}$$','3: Recognises integration pattern to obtain anti-derivative as a log function then evaluates; 2: Substantial progress eg. obtains anti-derivative and partially evaluates; 1: Some progress eg. obtains anti-derivative',1308,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Substantial progress, e.g. obtains anti-derivative and partially evaluates"], [1, "Some progress, e.g. obtains anti-derivative"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Recognises integration pattern to obtain anti-derivative as a log function then evaluates", "source_original": {"latex": "If $f(x)=\\dfrac{\\ln x}{x}$, then\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\dfrac{f''(x)}{f(x)}&=\\dfrac{1-\\ln x}{x^2}\\times\\dfrac{x}{\\ln x}\\\\ &=\\dfrac{1-\\ln x}{x\\ln x}\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\therefore\\ \\int_e^{e^2}\\dfrac{1-x}{x\\ln x}\\,dx&=\\left[\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{\\ln x}{x}\\right)\\right]_e^{e^2}\\\\ &=\\left[\\ln(\\ln x)-\\ln x\\right]_e^{e^2}\\\\ &=\\ln 2-\\ln 1-(2-1)\\\\ &=\\ln 2-1\\end{aligned}$$", "criteria": [[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Substantial progress, e.g. obtains anti-derivative and partially evaluates"], [1, "Some progress, e.g. obtains anti-derivative"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: integrand in the evaluation line read $\\dfrac{1-x}{x\\ln x}$."}');

