$$AB=\sqrt{85^2+33^2}=91.181\ldots$$
$$\text{Angle }DAB=\tan^{-1}\left(\dfrac{33}{85}\right)=21^\circ 13''$$
$$\text{Angle }CAB=90^\circ-26^\circ-21^\circ 13''=42^\circ 47''$$
$$\text{Angle }ACB=(360^\circ-321^\circ)+26^\circ=65^\circ\quad\text{(angles at a point and alternate angles)}$$
$$\text{Angle }ABC=180^\circ-65^\circ-42^\circ 47''=72^\circ 13''\quad\text{(angle sum of triangle }ABC\text{)}$$
By the sine rule:
$$AC=\dfrac{\sin 72^\circ 13''\times 91.181}{\sin 65^\circ}=95.800$$
$$BC=\dfrac{\sin 42^\circ 47''\times 91.181}{\sin 65^\circ}=68.335$$
Alternatively, $BC$ may be determined using the cosine rule:
$$BC=\sqrt{91.181^2+95.800^2-2\times 91.181\times 95.800\times\cos 42^\circ 47''}=68.335$$
Perimeter of triangle $ABC$:
$$91.181+95.800+68.335=255.316$$
The total distance travelled is 255 km, correct to the nearest kilometre.','5: Provides correct solution; 4: Determines the length of the other sides of triangle $ABC$ using sine or cosine rule; 3: Finds all angles in triangle $ABC$ and distance $AB$ or equivalent merit; 2: Finds both distance $AB$ and angle $DAB$, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds either distance $AB$ or angle $DAB$, or equivalent merit',1346,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[5, "Correct answer"], [4, "Determines the length of the other sides of triangle $ABC$ using sine or cosine rule"], [3, "Finds all angles in triangle $ABC$ and distance $AB$ or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds both distance $AB$ and angle $DAB$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds either distance $AB$ or angle $DAB$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution", "source_original": {"latex": "By Pythagoras'' theorem:\n$$AB=\\sqrt{85^2+33^2}=91.181\\ldots$$\n$$\\text{Angle }DAB=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{33}{85}\\right)=21^\\circ 13''$$\n$$\\text{Angle }CAB=90^\\circ-26^\\circ-21^\\circ 13''=42^\\circ 47''$$\n$$\\text{Angle }ACB=(360^\\circ-321^\\circ)+26^\\circ=65^\\circ\\quad\\text{(angles at a point and alternate angles)}$$\n$$\\text{Angle }ABC=180^\\circ-65^\\circ-42^\\circ 47''=72^\\circ 13''\\quad\\text{(angle sum of triangle }ABC\\text{)}$$\nBy the sine rule:\n$$AC=\\dfrac{\\sin 72^\\circ 13''\\times 91.181}{\\sin 65^\\circ}=95.800$$\n$$BC=\\dfrac{\\sin 42^\\circ 47''\\times 91.181}{\\sin 65^\\circ}=68.335$$\nAlternatively, $BC$ may be determined using the cosine rule:\n$$BC=\\sqrt{91.181^2+95.800^2-2\\times 91.181\\times 68.335\\times\\cos 42^\\circ 47''}=68.335$$\nPerimeter of triangle $ABC$:\n$$91.181+95.800+68.335=255.316$$\nThe total distance travelled is 255 km, correct to the nearest kilometre.", "criteria": [[5, "Correct answer"], [4, "Determines the length of the other sides of triangle $ABC$ using sine or cosine rule"], [3, "Finds all angles in triangle $ABC$ and distance $AB$ or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds both distance $AB$ and angle $DAB$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds either distance $AB$ or angle $DAB$, or equivalent merit"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: the cosine-rule line used $68.335$ in place of $95.800$."}');

