Conditions:

$\ln(x-1)$ is defined: $x-1>0$, so $x>1$.

The square root needs a non-negative input: $\ln(x-1)\ge 0$.
$$\begin{aligned} \ln(x-1)&\ge 0\\ x-1&\ge 1 \quad(\text{since } \ln 1=0 \text{ and } \ln \text{ is increasing})\\ x&\ge 2 \end{aligned}$$
$x\ge2$ also satisfies $x>1$.

$\therefore$ Domain: $[2,\infty)$','1: D',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"source_original": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$, $D: x\\ge0$\n\n$g(x)=\\ln(x-1)$, $D: x>1$\n\n$f(g(x))=\\sqrt{\\ln(x-1)}$\n\nWhen $x=2$, $\\sqrt{\\ln1}=0$\n\n$\\therefore\\ D: x\\ge 2$", "explained": true, "owner_note_round3": true}');
$$\begin{aligned} \int_1^a (x-1)\,dx &= 1 \\ \left[\dfrac{x^2}{2}-x\right]_1^a &= 1 \\ \left(\dfrac{a^2}{2}-a\right)-\left(\dfrac12-1\right) &= 1 \\ \dfrac{a^2}{2}-a-\dfrac12 &= 0 \\ a^2-2a-1 &= 0 \end{aligned}$$
The roots are
$$a=1\pm\sqrt2$$
The domain is $1\le x\le a$, so $a>1$. The smaller root $1-\sqrt2$ is negative, so $a$ is the larger root, $a=1+\sqrt2$.','1: A',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"source_original": "$$\\begin{aligned} \\int_1^a (x-1)\\,dx &= 1 \\\\ \\left[\\dfrac{x^2}{2}-x\\right]_1^a &= 1 \\\\ \\left(\\dfrac{a^2}{2}-a\\right)-\\left(\\dfrac12-1\\right) &= 1 \\\\ \\dfrac{a^2}{2}-a-\\dfrac12 &= 0 \\\\ a^2-2a-1 &= 0 \\end{aligned}$$", "explained": true, "owner_note_round3": true}');

For $y=\tan(nx)$ the period is $\dfrac{\pi}{n}$:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{\pi}{n}&=\dfrac{\pi}{2}\\ n&=2 \end{aligned}$$
The graph is $y=\tan 2x$ shifted $\dfrac{\pi}{4}$ to the left:
$$\begin{aligned} y &= \tan\left(2\left(x+\dfrac{\pi}{4}\right)\right) \\ &= \tan\left(2x+\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right) \end{aligned}$$','1: C',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"source_original": "$$p=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\quad n=\\dfrac{\\pi}{\\pi/2}=2$$\n$$\\begin{aligned} y &= \\tan\\left(2\\left(x+\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &= \\tan\\left(2x+\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\end{aligned}$$", "explained": true, "owner_note_round3": true}');
