$$\begin{aligned} x &= \dfrac{\ln32}{\ln2} \\ &= \dfrac{\ln2^5}{\ln2} \\ &= \dfrac{5\ln2}{\ln2} \\ &= 5 \end{aligned}$$','1: to realise the pattern; 1: to simplify. Done well!',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Recognises the cancelling pattern, or equivalent merit"]]','{"marker_note": "Done well!", "top_criterion_original": "To simplify", "criteria_original": [[1, "To realise the pattern"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov).", "source_original": "$$\\dfrac{\\log32}{\\log31}\\times\\dfrac{\\log31}{\\log30}\\times\\dfrac{\\log30}{\\log29}\\times\\cdots\\times\\dfrac{\\log4}{\\log3}\\times\\dfrac{\\log3}{\\log2}$$\nThe terms cancel, so\n$$\\begin{aligned} x &= \\dfrac{\\log32}{\\log2} \\\\ &= \\dfrac{\\log2^5}{\\log2^1} \\\\ &= 5 \\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\therefore\\ x=5$$", "explained": true, "owner_note_round3": true}');
