Substitute $y=mx+2$ into $(y+1)$:
$$\begin{aligned} (x-2)^2+(mx+2+1)^2 &= 9 \\ x^2-4x+4+m^2x^2+6mx+9 &= 9 \\ x^2+m^2x^2-4x+6mx+4+9-9 &= 0 \\ x^2(1+m^2)+x(6m-4)+4 &= 0 \end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} (6m-4)^2-4(m^2+1)(4) &= 0 \\ 36m^2-48m+16-16m^2-16 &= 0 \\ 20m^2-48m &= 0 \\ 4m(5m-12) &= 0 \end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\ m=0 \text{ or } m=\dfrac{12}{5}$$','1: discriminant equation $(6m-4)^2-4(m^2+1)(4)=0$; 1: both solutions. Comments: mistake with $m^2x^2$ (many students wrote $mx^2$); when factorising $20m^2-48m=0$ students didn''t write $4m$.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Forms the discriminant equation $(6m-4)^2-4(m^2+1)(4)=0$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"marker_note": "Comments: mistake with $m^2x^2$ (many students wrote $mx^2$); when factorising $20m^2-48m=0$, students didn''t write $4m$.", "top_criterion_original": "Both solutions", "criteria_original": [[1, "Discriminant equation $(6m-4)^2-4(m^2+1)(4)=0$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
