$$\therefore\ x=-\pi,\ 0,\ 0.615,\ 2.526,\ \pi$$','1: $x=-\pi,0,\pi$; 1: $0.615, 2.5262$. Mistakes: missed all solutions for $\sin x=0$; gave answers in degrees; gave answers in wrong quadrants and not 3 d.p.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Obtains $x=-\\pi,0,\\pi$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"marker_note": "Mistakes: missed all solutions for $\\sin x=0$; gave answers in degrees; gave answers in wrong quadrants and not 3 d.p.", "top_criterion_original": "$0.615$, $2.5262$", "source_original": {"latex": "$$\\sin x(3\\sin x-\\sqrt3)=0$$\n$\\sin x=0$:\n$$\\therefore\\ x=-\\pi,\\ 0,\\ \\pi$$\n$3\\sin x=\\sqrt3$:\n$$\\begin{aligned} x &= \\sin^{-1}\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{3} \\\\ &= 0.615,\\ 2.5262 \\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\therefore\\ x=-\\pi,\\ 0,\\ 0.615,\\ 2.5262,\\ \\pi$$", "criteria": [[1, "$x=-\\pi,0,\\pi$"], [1, "Correct answer"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: the second solution was given to 4 decimal places ($2.5262$).", "criteria_original": [[1, "$x=-\\pi,0,\\pi$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
