$$\begin{aligned} u&=e^x & v&=\sin x\\ u''&=e^x & v''&=\cos x\end{aligned}$$
For $e^x\cos x$:
$$\begin{aligned} u&=e^x & v&=\cos x\\ u''&=e^x & v''&=-\sin x\end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} g''(x) &= \sin x\cdot e^x+e^x\cos x-[\cos x\cdot e^x+e^x(-\sin x)] \\ &= e^x\sin x+e^x\cos x-e^x\cos x+e^x\sin x \\ &= 2e^x\sin x \end{aligned}$$','1: $2e^x\sin x$. Some students made mistake with the negative sign.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"marker_note": "Some students made mistake with the negative sign.", "top_criterion_original": "$2e^x\\sin x$", "source_original": {"latex": "$$\\begin{aligned} g''(x) &= \\sin x\\cdot e^x+e^x\\cos x-[\\cos x\\cdot e^x+e^x(-\\sin x)] \\\\ &= e^x\\sin x+e^x\\cos x-e^x\\cos x+e^x\\sin x \\\\ &= 2e^x\\sin x \\end{aligned}$$"}}');
