$$\therefore\ f(x)=\dfrac12(e^x\sin x-e^x\cos x)$$','No marks breakdown shown (2 marks).',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[null, "No marks breakdown shown (2 marks)."]]','{}');
$$1+\dfrac13,\quad 2+\dfrac19,\quad 4+\dfrac1{27},\quad 8+\dfrac1{81},\ \ldots$$
The whole numbers $1,2,4,8,\ldots$ form a GP with $a_1=1$, $r_1=2$.

The fractions $\dfrac13,\dfrac19,\dfrac1{27},\dfrac1{81},\ldots$ form a second GP with $a_2=\dfrac13$, $r_2=\dfrac13$.

So the general term is the sum of the general terms of the two GPs:
$$\begin{aligned} T_n &= a_1r_1^{n-1}+a_2r_2^{n-1} \\ &= 1(2)^{n-1}+\dfrac13\left(\dfrac13\right)^{n-1} \\ &= 2^{n-1}+\dfrac{1}{3^n} \end{aligned}$$','1: understanding 2 separate GP''s; 1: general term.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Recognises two separate geometric progressions, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "General term", "criteria_original": [[1, "Understanding 2 separate GPs"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov).", "source_original": "$GP_1=1+2+4+8+\\cdots$, with $a_1=1$, $r_1=2$.\n\n$$GP_2=\\dfrac13+\\dfrac19+\\dfrac1{27}+\\dfrac1{81}+\\cdots$$\nwith $a_2=\\dfrac13$, $r_2=\\dfrac13$.\n$$\\begin{aligned} T_n &= a_1r_1^{n-1}+a_2r_2^{n-1} \\\\ &= 1(2)^{n-1}+\\dfrac13\\left(\\dfrac13\\right)^{n-1} \\\\ &= 2^{n-1}+\\dfrac{1}{3^n} \\end{aligned}$$", "explained": true, "owner_note_round3": true}');
$$\therefore\ S_n=2^n-\dfrac12\left(\dfrac{1}{3^n}\right)-\dfrac12 \text{ or } \dfrac{2^{n+1}-3^{-n}-1}{2}$$','1: $2^n-1+\frac12-\frac12(\frac1{3^n})$; 1: simplified final answer. Have to simplify to get the 2nd mark!',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Obtains $2^n-1+\\dfrac12-\\dfrac12\\left(\\dfrac1{3^n}\\right)$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"marker_note": "Have to simplify to get the 2nd mark!", "top_criterion_original": "Simplified final answer", "criteria_original": [[1, "$2^n-1+\\dfrac12-\\dfrac12\\left(\\dfrac1{3^n}\\right)$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');

