$$f(2)=8-24+18+1=3$$
$\therefore$ Point of inflexion at $(2,3)$.','1 mark for: $f''''(x)=6x-12=0$, $x=2$, P.O.I is $(2,3)$. 1 mark for testing: $f''''(1)=-6<0$ and $f''''(3)=6>0$. When testing, the final value must be shown, i.e. $f''''(3)>0$ is insufficient. Students must test the second derivative for the concavity.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Solves $f''''(x)=0$ to get $x=2$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"marker_note": "Students must test the second derivative for the concavity. When testing, the final value must be shown, i.e. $f''''(3)>0$ is insufficient.", "top_criterion_original": "Testing: $f''''(1)=-6<0$ and $f''''(3)=6>0$", "criteria_original": [[1, "$f''''(x)=6x-12=0$, $x=2$, P.O.I. is $(2,3)$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov).", "source_original": "$$\\begin{aligned} f''''(x)=6x-12 &= 0 \\\\ x &= 2 \\end{aligned}$$\nP.O.I. is $(2,3)$.\n\nTesting:\n$$\\begin{aligned} f''''(1) &= -6<0 &&\\text{concave down} \\\\ f''''(3) &= 6>0 &&\\text{concave up} \\end{aligned}$$", "explained": true, "owner_note_round3": true}');

The total area under the curve is $1$ and the area between $-N$ and $N$ is $p$, so the two tails together have area $1-p$. By symmetry each tail has area $\dfrac{1-p}{2}$.
$$\begin{aligned} P(z<N) &= 1-\dfrac{1-p}{2} \\ &= \dfrac12+\dfrac{p}{2} \end{aligned}$$','1: correct expression. Overall, students did well.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"marker_note": "Overall, students did well.", "top_criterion_original": "Correct expression", "source_original": "Normal curve sketch with shaded area $p$ between $-N$ and $N$.\n$$\\therefore\\ P(z<N)=\\dfrac12+\\dfrac{p}{2}$$", "explained": true, "owner_note_round3": true}');
