$$\begin{aligned} f''(x) &= \dfrac{2\cos x}{\sin x}+\dfrac{2\sin x}{\cos x} \\ &= \dfrac{2\cos^2x+2\sin^2x}{\sin x\cos x} \\ &= \dfrac{2(\cos^2x+\sin^2x)}{\sin x\cos x} \\ &= \dfrac{2}{\sin x\cos x} \end{aligned}$$','1 mark for differentiation. 1 mark for using any trig identities. 1 mark for simplifying the final answer.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Uses a relevant trigonometric identity, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Differentiates correctly, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Simplifying the final answer", "criteria_original": [[1, "Differentiation"], [1, "Using any trig identities"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
