$$\therefore\ F(x)=\begin{cases}0, & x<0\\ 2\left(1-e^{-\frac12x}\right), & 0\le x\le\ln4\\ 1, & x\ge\ln4\end{cases}$$','1: $2(1-e^{-\frac12x})$; 1: full piecewise CDF. Students did well.',1365,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Obtains $2\\left(1-e^{-\\frac12x}\\right)$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"marker_note": "Students did well.", "top_criterion_original": "Full piecewise CDF", "source_original": {"latex": "$$\\begin{aligned} \\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\int_0^x e^{-\\frac12x}\\,dx &= -2\\left(e^{-\\frac12x}-1\\right) \\text{ or } 2\\left(1-e^{-\\frac12x}\\right) \\\\ &= -2e^{-\\frac12x}+2 \\\\ &= 2-2e^{-\\frac12x} \\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\therefore\\ F(x)=\\begin{cases}0, & x<0\\\\ -2\\left(1-e^{-\\frac12x}\\right), & 0\\le x\\le\\ln4\\\\ 1, & x\\ge\\ln4\\end{cases}$$", "criteria": [[1, "$2\\left(1-e^{-\\frac12x}\\right)$"], [1, "Correct answer"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: the middle piece of $F(x)$ had a wrong minus sign, and a spurious limit stood in front of the integral.", "criteria_original": [[1, "$2\\left(1-e^{-\\frac12x}\\right)$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
