We want $B_n < 0$.

Find $n$ so that $B_n = 0$.
$$\begin{aligned} 30\,025.83(1.03)^n &= 2000\left[\dfrac{(1.03)^n - 1}{1.03 - 1}\right] \\ \dfrac{0.03\times 30\,025.83}{2000}(1.03)^n &= (1.03)^n - 1 \\ 0.45039(1.03)^n &= (1.03)^n - 1 \\ 0.54961(1.03)^n &= 1 \\ (1.03)^n &= 1.8194\ldots \\ n\ln(1.03) &= \ln(1.8194) \\ n &= \dfrac{\ln(1.8194)}{\ln(1.03)} \\ n &\approx 20.25 \end{aligned}$$
