$$y = x^2 - 1$$
$$y'' = 2x$$
Gradient of tangent at $x = a$ is $2a$.

$\therefore$ Equation of tangent at $(a, a^2 - 1)$ is
$$\begin{aligned} y - \left(a^2 - 1\right) &= 2a(x - a) \\ y - a^2 + 1 &= 2ax - 2a^2 \\ y &= 2ax - a^2 - 1 \end{aligned}$$
Since the tangent passes through $(3, -8)$, then
$$\begin{aligned} -8 &= 6a - a^2 - 1 \\ a^2 - 6a - 7 &= 0 \\ (a-7)(a+1) &= 0 \\ a &= 7 \text{ or } a = -1 \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ The equations of the two tangents are:

When $a = 7$,
$$\begin{aligned} y &= 2(7)x - 7^2 - 1 \\ y &= 14x - 50 \end{aligned}$$
and when $a = -1$,
$$\begin{aligned} y &= 2(-1)x - (-1)^2 - 1 \\ y &= -2x - 2 \end{aligned}$$','4: Provides correct solution; 3: Substitute $(3, -8)$ into the equation of the tangent at $x = a$, or equivalent merit; 2: Finds the equation of the tangent at $x = a$, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds the gradient of the tangent at $x = a$, or equivalent merit',226,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Substitute $(3, -8)$ into the equation of the tangent at $x = a$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds the equation of the tangent at $x = a$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the gradient of the tangent at $x = a$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
