Alternate solution
$$g(x) = k(x - m)^2 - 5$$
$$\begin{aligned} g(x) &= 3x^2 - 12x + 7 \\ &= 3\left(x^2 - 4x\right) + 7 \\ &= 3\left(x^2 - 4x + 4\right) + 7 - 12 \\ &= 3(x - 2)^2 - 5 \end{aligned}$$
So $k = 3$ and $m = 2$.','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Writes g(x) in terms of m and k, and finds value of k, or equivalent merit; 1: Writes g(x) in terms of m and k, or equivalent merit',267,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Writes $g(x)$ in terms of $m$ and $k$, and finds value of $k$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Writes $g(x)$ in terms of $m$ and $k$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
