In $\triangle MTC$, $\angle TMC=28^\circ$ from part (a) and $TC\approx58$ from part (b). Use the sine rule to find $\angle MTC$:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{\sin\angle MTC}{97} &= \dfrac{\sin 28^\circ}{58} \\ \sin\angle MTC &= \dfrac{97}{58}\sin 28^\circ \end{aligned}$$
$$\angle MTC \approx 51.73^\circ \text{ or } 180^\circ - 51.73^\circ \approx 128.27^\circ$$
$\because$ $MC$ is the longest side,
$$\therefore \angle MTC \approx 128.27^\circ$$
(so that $\angle TCM$ is acute).
$$247^\circ - 128.27^\circ = 118.73^\circ \approx 119^\circ\text{T}$$
$\therefore$ the bearing of $C$ from $T$ is $119^\circ\text{T}$.

Method 2: By cosine rule,
$$\cos\angle MTC = \dfrac{50^2 + 58^2 - 97^2}{2(50)(58)}=-0.611\ldots$$
$$\angle MTC \approx 127.7^\circ,\qquad 247^\circ - 127.7^\circ \approx 119^\circ\text{T}$$','1: $\angle MTC \doteq 128.27^\circ$ (must justify the obtuse angle); 1: correct bearing $119^\circ$T',409,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Obtains $\\angle MTC \\approx 128.27^\\circ$ (must justify the obtuse angle), or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Correct bearing $119^\\circ\\text{T}$", "source_original": {"latex": "$$\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{\\sin\\angle MTC}{97} &= \\dfrac{\\sin 28^\\circ}{58} \\\\ \\sin\\angle MTC &= \\dfrac{97}{58}\\sin 28^\\circ \\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\angle MTC \\approx 51.73^\\circ \\text{ or } 180^\\circ - 51.73^\\circ \\approx 128.27^\\circ$$\n$\\because$ $MC$ is the longest side,\n$$\\therefore \\angle MTC \\approx 128.27^\\circ$$\n(so that $\\angle TCM$ is acute).\n$$247^\\circ - 128.27^\\circ = 118.73^\\circ \\approx 119^\\circ\\text{T}$$\n$\\therefore$ the bearing of $C$ from $T$ is $119^\\circ\\text{T}$.\n\nMethod 2: By cosine rule,\n$$\\cos\\angle MTC = \\dfrac{50^2 + 58^2 - 97^2}{2(50)(58)}\\ldots$$", "criteria": [[1, "$\\angle MTC \\approx 128.27^\\circ$ (must justify the obtuse angle)"], [1, "Correct answer"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: Method 2 stopped part-way in the source; completed.", "criteria_original": [[1, "$\\angle MTC \\approx 128.27^\\circ$ (must justify the obtuse angle)"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov).", "explained": "Diagram and set-up sentence added by Claude (owner request, 11 Nov)."}');
