$$\begin{aligned} u&=x & v&=e^{-x^2}\\ u''&=1 & v''&=-2xe^{-x^2}\end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} f''(x) &= x\left(-2xe^{-x^2}\right) + e^{-x^2} \\ &= (1-2x^2)e^{-x^2} \end{aligned}$$
Stationary points occur when $f''(x) = 0$:
$$\begin{aligned} (1-2x^2)e^{-x^2} &= 0 \\ 1 - 2x^2 &= 0 \\ x^2 &= \dfrac{1}{2} \\ x &= \dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \text{ or } x = -\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \end{aligned}$$
When $x = \dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$:
$$f\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\right) = \dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}e^{-\frac{1}{2}} = \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2e}}$$
When $x = -\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$:
$$f\left(-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\right) = \left(-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\right)e^{-\frac{1}{2}} = -\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2e}}$$
$\therefore$ The stationary points are
$$\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}, \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2e}}\right)$$
and
$$\left(-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}, -\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2e}}\right)$$','1: $f''(x) = (1-2x^2)e^{-x^2}$; 1: $x = \pm\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$; 1: correct coordinates',409,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Obtains $x = \\pm\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Obtains $f''(x) = (1-2x^2)e^{-x^2}$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Correct coordinates", "criteria_original": [[1, "$f''(x) = (1-2x^2)e^{-x^2}$"], [1, "$x = \\pm\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov).", "source_original": {"latex": "Let $f(x) = uv$ with $u = x$, $u'' = 1$, $v = e^{-x^2}$, $v'' = -2xe^{-x^2}$.\n$$\\begin{aligned} f''(x) &= x\\left(-2xe^{-x^2}\\right) + e^{-x^2} \\\\ &= (1-2x^2)e^{-x^2} \\end{aligned}$$\nStationary points occur when $f''(x) = 0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned} (1-2x^2)e^{-x^2} &= 0 \\\\ 1 - 2x^2 &= 0 \\\\ x^2 &= \\dfrac{1}{2} \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\text{ or } x = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\end{aligned}$$\nWhen $x = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$:\n$$f\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}e^{-\\frac{1}{2}} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2e}}$$\nWhen $x = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$:\n$$f\\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) = \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)e^{-\\frac{1}{2}} = -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2e}}$$\n$\\therefore$ The stationary points are\n$$\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2e}}\\right)$$\nand\n$$\\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}, -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2e}}\\right)$$"}}');
$$\begin{aligned} f(x) = \dfrac{x}{e^{x^2}} &\to 0^+ &&\text{as } x \to \infty\\ f(x) = \dfrac{x}{e^{x^2}} &\to 0^- &&\text{as } x \to -\infty \end{aligned}$$

