$$r^2 = h^2 + d^2$$
$\phi$ is the angle at $A$, and the side opposite it is $h$:
$$\sin\phi = \dfrac{h}{r} = \dfrac{h}{\sqrt{h^2+d^2}}$$
Substitute both into $I = \dfrac{C\sin\phi}{r^2}$ to write $I$ in terms of $h$ only:
$$\begin{aligned} I &= C\left(\dfrac{h}{\sqrt{h^2+d^2}}\right)\left(\dfrac{1}{h^2+d^2}\right) \\ &= Ch(h^2+d^2)^{-\frac{3}{2}} \end{aligned}$$
Differentiate using the product rule:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{dI}{dh} &= C(h^2+d^2)^{-\frac{3}{2}} + Ch\left(-\dfrac{3}{2}\right)(2h)(h^2+d^2)^{-\frac{5}{2}} \\ &= C(h^2+d^2)^{-\frac{5}{2}}\left[(h^2+d^2) - 3h^2\right] \\ &= C(h^2+d^2)^{-\frac{5}{2}}(d^2 - 2h^2) \end{aligned}$$
Since $C>0$ and $(h^2+d^2)^{-\frac{5}{2}}>0$, $\dfrac{dI}{dh}=0$ when
$$\begin{aligned} d^2 - 2h^2 &= 0 \\ h^2 &= \dfrac{d^2}{2} \\ h &= \dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}d \quad (h>0) \end{aligned}$$
The sign of $\dfrac{dI}{dh}$ is the sign of $d^2-2h^2$. Test either side:
$$\begin{aligned} h &= \dfrac{d}{2}: & d^2-2\left(\dfrac{d}{2}\right)^2 &= \dfrac{d^2}{2} > 0 \\ h &= d: & d^2-2d^2 &= -d^2 < 0 \end{aligned}$$
$I$ increases then decreases, so the stationary point is a maximum.

$\therefore$ The intensity at $A$ is greatest when $h = \dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}d$.','1: suitable substitution $\sin\phi = \dfrac{h}{\sqrt{h^2+a^2}}$; 1: $I = Ch(h^2+a^2)^{-\frac{3}{2}}$; 1: $\dfrac{dI}{dh} = C(h^2+a^2)^{-\frac{5}{2}}(a^2-2h^2)$; 1: $h = \dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}a$; 1: verifying maximum',409,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[5, "Correct answer"], [4, "Obtains $h = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}d$, or equivalent merit"], [3, "Obtains $\\dfrac{dI}{dh} = C(h^2+d^2)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}(d^2-2h^2)$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Obtains $I = Ch(h^2+d^2)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Makes a suitable substitution, $\\sin\\phi=\\dfrac{h}{\\sqrt{h^2+d^2}}$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Verifying maximum", "source_original": {"latex": "$$I = \\dfrac{C\\sin\\phi}{r^2}$$\n$$r^2 = h^2 + a^2, \\qquad \\sin\\phi = \\dfrac{h}{r} = \\dfrac{h}{\\sqrt{h^2+a^2}}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned} I &= C\\left(\\dfrac{h}{\\sqrt{h^2+a^2}}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{1}{h^2+a^2}\\right) \\\\ &= Ch(h^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{3}{2}} \\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{dI}{dh} &= C(h^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{3}{2}} + C\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right)(2h)(h^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}h \\\\ &= C(h^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}\\left[(h^2+a^2) - 3h^2\\right] \\\\ &= C(h^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}(a^2 - 2h^2) \\end{aligned}$$\nWhen $\\dfrac{dI}{dh} = 0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned} a^2 - 2h^2 &= 0 \\\\ h^2 &= \\dfrac{a^2}{2} \\\\ h &= \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}a \\quad \\left(\\text{reject } h = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}a\\right) \\end{aligned}$$\nTest the sign of $\\dfrac{dI}{dh}$ either side:\n$$\\begin{aligned} h &= \\dfrac{1}{2}a: & \\dfrac{dI}{dh} &= C\\left(\\left(\\dfrac{a}{2}\\right)^2 + a^2\\right)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}\\left(a^2 - 2\\left(\\dfrac{a}{2}\\right)^2\\right) = C\\left(\\dfrac{5}{4}a^2\\right)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}a^2\\right) > 0 &&\\text{increasing}\\\\ h &= a: & \\dfrac{dI}{dh} &= C(a^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}(a^2 - 2a^2) < 0 &&\\text{decreasing} \\end{aligned}$$\n$\\therefore$ When $h = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}a$, the intensity $I$ is maximised.", "criteria": [[1, "Suitable substitution $\\sin\\phi = \\dfrac{h}{\\sqrt{h^2+a^2}}$"], [1, "$I = Ch(h^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}$"], [1, "$\\dfrac{dI}{dh} = C(h^2+a^2)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}(a^2-2h^2)$"], [1, "$h = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}a$"], [1, "Correct answer"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: the question calls the distance $OA$ $d$, but the source solution used $a$; changed to $d$ throughout.", "criteria_original": [[1, "Suitable substitution $\\sin\\phi = \\dfrac{h}{\\sqrt{h^2+d^2}}$"], [1, "$I = Ch(h^2+d^2)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}$"], [1, "$\\dfrac{dI}{dh} = C(h^2+d^2)^{-\\frac{5}{2}}(d^2-2h^2)$"], [1, "$h = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}d$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov).", "explained": "Working explained in words (owner request, 11 Nov)."}');
