$$h(x) = -3^{-x} + b = -\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^x + b$$
For the $y$-intercept, $x = 0$: $h(0) = b - 1$.

For the $x$-intercept:
$$\begin{aligned} -\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^x + b &= 0 \\ b &= \left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^x \\ x &= \log_{\frac{1}{3}} b = -\log_3 b \end{aligned}$$
\exfigure{408_q32_s1}','1: intercepts; 1: shape + asymptote',409,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds the intercepts, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Shape and asymptote", "criteria_original": [[1, "Intercepts"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
$$\begin{aligned} \text{LHS} &= \left[\dfrac{3^{-x}}{\ln 3} + bx\right]_{-\log_3 b}^{0} \\ &= \left(\dfrac{3^0}{\ln 3} + 0\right) - \left(\dfrac{3^{\log_3 b}}{\ln 3} - b\log_3 b\right) \\ &= \dfrac{1}{\ln 3} - \dfrac{b}{\ln 3} + b\log_3 b \end{aligned}$$
LHS = RHS:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{1}{\ln 3} - \dfrac{b}{\ln 3} + b\log_3 b &= \dfrac{1}{\ln 3} \\ -\dfrac{b}{\ln 3} + b\log_3 b &= 0 \\ b\log_3 b &= \dfrac{b}{\ln 3} \end{aligned}$$
Since $b \ne 0$:
$$\begin{aligned} \log_3 b &= \dfrac{1}{\ln 3} \\ \dfrac{\ln b}{\ln 3} &= \dfrac{1}{\ln 3} \\ \ln b &= 1 \end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\ b = e$$','1: primitive; 1: $\dfrac{1}{\ln 3} - \dfrac{b}{\ln 3} + b\log_3 b$; 1: $b = e$',409,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Obtains $\\dfrac{1}{\\ln 3} - \\dfrac{b}{\\ln 3} + b\\log_3 b$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the primitive, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "$b = e$", "criteria_original": [[1, "Primitive"], [1, "$\\dfrac{1}{\\ln 3} - \\dfrac{b}{\\ln 3} + b\\log_3 b$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
