$$\begin{aligned} 3a &= 33 \\ a &= 11 \end{aligned}$$
Product: $a(a-d)(a+d) = 1232$
$$\begin{aligned} a(a^2 - d^2) &= 1232 \\ 11(11^2 - d^2) &= 1232 \\ 121 - d^2 &= 112 \\ 9 &= d^2 \\ d &= \pm 3 \end{aligned}$$
When $d = 3$: $11 - 3, 11, 11 + 3$, i.e. $8, 11, 14$.

When $d = -3$: $11 + 3, 11, 11 - 3$, i.e. $14, 11, 8$.

$\therefore$ The terms are $8, 11, 14$.','1: $d = \pm 3$; 1: terms 8, 11, 14',642,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Obtains $d = \\pm 3$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"top_criterion_original": "Terms $8, 11, 14$", "criteria_original": [[1, "$d = \\pm 3$"], [1, "Correct answer"]], "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
