$$\begin{aligned} F(t) &= \int R\,dt \\ &= \int 5+4e^{-0.5t}\,dt \\ &= 5t-8e^{-0.5t}+c \end{aligned}$$

At time $t=1$, the vehicle has consumed 25 litres of fuel since the start of the journey.

Finding the constant of integration, $c$:
$$\begin{aligned} 25 &= 5(1)-8e^{-0.5(1)}+c \\ 20 &= -8e^{-0.5}+c \\ c &= 20+8e^{-0.5} \end{aligned}$$

At time $t=4$, the amount of fuel the vehicle consumed is given by
$$\begin{aligned} F &= 5(4)-8e^{-0.5(4)}+20+8e^{-0.5} \\ &= 43.7695\ldots \end{aligned}$$

$\therefore$ After 4 hours of travel, the vehicle has consumed 44 litres of fuel.','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Finds the value of the constant of integration, or equivalent merit; 1: Correctly integrates expression representing rate of fuel consumption, or equivalent merit [reused from duplicate 61]',1346,NULL,'dup-reuse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds the value of the constant of integration, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly integrates expression representing rate of fuel consumption, or equivalent merit"]]','{"reused_from": 61, "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
