$$\begin{aligned} h &= \sqrt{\dfrac{39x^2}{4}} \\ &= \dfrac{\sqrt{39}\,x}{2} \end{aligned}$$','2: Provides correct solution; 1: Attempts to use Pythagoras'' theorem to find $h$, or equivalent merit [reused from duplicate question 66, similarity 0.93]',1346,NULL,'dup-reuse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Attempts to use Pythagoras'' theorem to find $h$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"reused_from": 66, "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');

Let $A$ be the area of the cross-section of the tent.
$$\begin{aligned} A &= 5xy+\dfrac{1}{2}\times 5x\times h \\ &= 5xy+\dfrac{5xh}{2} \end{aligned}$$

From parts (a) and (b):
$$\begin{aligned} A &= 5x(10-4x)+\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}x^2}{4} \\ &= 50x-20x^2+\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}x^2}{4} \\ &= 50x-\left(20-\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}}{4}\right)x^2 \end{aligned}$$

Determine the stationary point and its nature:
$$\dfrac{dA}{dx}=50-2\left(20-\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}}{4}\right)x$$

$$\begin{aligned} 50-2\left(20-\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}}{4}\right)x &= 0 \\ \left(20-\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}}{4}\right)x &= 25 \\ x &= 25\div\left(20-\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}}{4}\right) \\ &= 2.05 \end{aligned}$$

$$\dfrac{d^2A}{dx^2}=-2\left(20-\dfrac{5\sqrt{39}}{4}\right)=-24.387\ldots<0$$

$\therefore$ Maximum volume at $x=2.05$.','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Finds stationary point, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds correct expression for surface area of tent, or equivalent merit [reused from duplicate question 66, similarity 0.93]',1346,NULL,'dup-reuse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds stationary point, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds correct expression for area of the cross-section of the tent, or equivalent merit"]]','{"reused_from": 66, "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution", "source_original": {"latex": "Maximise the volume by maximising the area of the cross-section, since the depth is constant.\n\nLet $A$ be the area of the cross-section of the tent.\n$$\\begin{aligned} A &= 5xy+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\times 5x\\times h \\\\ &= 5xy+\\dfrac{5xh}{2} \\end{aligned}$$\n\nFrom parts (a) and (b):\n$$\\begin{aligned} A &= 5x(10-4x)+\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}x^2}{4} \\\\ &= 50x-20x^2+\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}x^2}{4} \\\\ &= 50x-\\left(20-\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}}{4}\\right)x^2 \\end{aligned}$$\n\nDetermine the stationary point and its nature:\n$$\\dfrac{dA}{dx}=50-2\\left(20-\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}}{4}\\right)x$$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned} 50-2\\left(20-\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}}{4}\\right)x &= 0 \\\\ \\left(20-\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}}{4}\\right)x &= 25 \\\\ x &= 25\\div\\left(20-\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}}{4}\\right) \\\\ &= 2.05 \\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\dfrac{d^2A}{dx^2}=-2\\left(20-\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{39}}{4}\\right)=-24.387\\ldots<0$$\n\n$\\therefore$ Maximum volume at $x=2.05$.", "criteria": [[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds stationary point, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds correct expression for surface area of tent, or equivalent merit"]]}, "corrected": "Corrected from source: the 1-mark criterion said \"surface area\"; the working finds the cross-sectional area."}');

