For $0 \le x \le 1$ the parabola $y = (x-1)^2$ is above the line $y = 2x - 2$, so the area is
$$\int_0^1\big((x-1)^2 - (2x-2)\big)dx = \int_0^1\big((x-1)^2 - 2x + 2\big)dx$$

For $1 \le x \le 3$ the line is above the parabola (they meet at $(1, 0)$ and $(3, 4)$), so the area is
$$\int_1^3\big((2x-2) - (x-1)^2\big)dx$$

Total area:
$$\int_0^1\big((x-1)^2 - 2x + 2\big)dx + \int_1^3\big((2x-2) - (x-1)^2\big)dx$$','1: upper minus lower on [0,1] and on [1,3]: option D [confidence 0.9; check: passed] CONCERN: Options A and C are printed identically in the source; this does not affect the answer D.',NULL,'claude-opus-5-5 (subagent)','gen-v1','human:approved','2026-11-11T00:05:15.183Z','[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"confidence": 0.9, "check": "passed"}');
