hes $0$ at $t \\approx 3.39$ minutes, so under this model the pool is empty ($0 \\text{ m}^3$) before $4$ minutes.\n\nIf the question meant water flowing into the pool at this rate, then\n$$V(4) = 10 + \\dfrac{32}{3} = \\dfrac{62}{3} \\approx 20.7 \\text{ m}^3$$"}, "corrected": "Question adapted so it can be solved: the paper starts the pool at $10$ m$^3$, but $\\dfrac{32}{3}$ m$^3$ flows out in $4$ minutes, which would empty it. The starting volume is now $20$ m$^3$."}');
