Differentiating:
$$\begin{aligned} y &= x^4-2x^3+2\\ y'' &= 4x^3-6x^2\\ y'''' &= 12x^2-12x\end{aligned}$$
Stationary points occur where $y''=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} 4x^3-6x^2 &= 0\\ 2x^2(2x-3) &= 0\end{aligned}$$
$$x=0 \text{ or } x=\dfrac{3}{2}$$
When $x=0$, $y=2$ and $y''''=0$. Check concavity:

\extable{Ts556_1}

Concavity changes sign, $\therefore$ horizontal point of inflection at $(0,2)$.

When $x=\dfrac{3}{2}$, $y=\dfrac{5}{16}$ and $y''''=9>0$.

$\therefore$ Local minimum at $\left(\dfrac{3}{2},\dfrac{5}{16}\right)$.

Possible points of inflection occur where $y''''=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} 12x^2-12x &= 0\\ 12x(x-1) &= 0\end{aligned}$$
$$x=0 \text{ or } x=1$$
$(0,2)$ is already found. When $x=1$, $y=1$. Check concavity:

\extable{Ts556_2}

Concavity changes sign, $\therefore$ point of inflection at $(1,1)$.','5: Provides correct graph; 4: Correctly identifies all points of inflection and stationary points; 3: Finds the nature of the stationary points; 2: Finds the $x$ values of both stationary points, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds the first derivative, or equivalent merit',1628,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[5, "Correct answer"], [4, "Correctly identifies all points of inflection and stationary points, or equivalent merit"], [3, "Finds the nature of the stationary points, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds the $x$ values of both stationary points, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the first derivative, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[5, "Provides correct graph"], [4, "Correctly identifies all points of inflection and stationary points"], [3, "Finds the nature of the stationary points"], [2, "Finds the $x$ values of both stationary points, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the first derivative, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct graph"}');
