The first deposit accrues interest for 24 months.

$\therefore$ Its future value is $80(1.005)^{24}$.

The next deposit accrues interest for 23 months, and so on, down to 1 month for the last deposit.

Summing the geometric series ($a=1.005$, $r=1.005$, 24 terms):
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Total} &= 80(1.005)^{24}+80(1.005)^{23}+\cdots+80(1.005)^{1}\\ &= 80\left[(1.005)^1+(1.005)^2+\cdots+(1.005)^{24}\right]\\ &= 80\times(1.005)\left[\dfrac{(1.005)^{24}-1}{1.005-1}\right]\\ &= 2044.73\end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ Jack will have $\$2044.73$.','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Sets up an appropriate series, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds a correct term in the series, or equivalent merit',1628,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Sets up an appropriate series, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds a correct term in the series, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Provides correct solution"], [2, "Sets up an appropriate series, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds a correct term in the series, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
