$$c-k\cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{24}t\right)=c-k\cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{24}(t-6)\right)$$
$$\therefore\ \cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{24}t\right)=\cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{24}(t-6)\right)$$
Two angles have equal cosines when they are equal, opposite, or add to $2\pi$ (within one revolution).

Equal angles:
$$\dfrac{\pi}{24}t=\dfrac{\pi}{24}(t-6)$$
which is impossible.

Opposite angles:
$$\begin{aligned} -\dfrac{\pi}{24}t &= \dfrac{\pi}{24}(t-6)\\ -\dfrac{\pi}{24}t &= \dfrac{\pi}{24}t-\dfrac{\pi}{4}\\ \dfrac{\pi}{12}t &= \dfrac{\pi}{4}\\ t &= 3\end{aligned}$$
Angles adding to $2\pi$:
$$\begin{aligned} 2\pi-\dfrac{\pi}{24}t &= \dfrac{\pi}{24}(t-6)\\ -\dfrac{2\pi}{24}t &= -2\pi-\dfrac{\pi}{4}\\ \dfrac{\pi t}{12} &= \dfrac{9\pi}{4}\\ t &= 27\end{aligned}$$
When $t=3$:
$$\text{height}=21-18\cos\dfrac{3\pi}{24}=4.37 \text{ m}$$
When $t=27$:
$$\text{height}=21-18\cos\dfrac{27\pi}{24}=37.63 \text{ m}$$','4: Provides a correct solution; 3: Finds $t=3$, or equivalent merit; 2: Makes correct use of the periodic nature of cosine function; 1: Equates the appropriate trigonometric ratios, or equivalent merit',1628,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Finds $t=3$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Makes correct use of the periodic nature of cosine function, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Equates the appropriate trigonometric ratios, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[4, "Provides a correct solution"], [3, "Finds $t=3$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Makes correct use of the periodic nature of cosine function"], [1, "Equates the appropriate trigonometric ratios, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides a correct solution"}');
