$$\begin{aligned} P &= 1\theta+(1+x)\theta+2x\\ &= (2+x)\theta+2x\end{aligned}$$
The area is the difference of two sectors ($A=\dfrac{1}{2}r^2\theta$):
$$\begin{aligned} A &= \dfrac{1}{2}(1+x)^2\theta-\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot 1^2\theta\\ &= \dfrac{1}{2}\theta\left[1+2x+x^2-1\right]\\ &= \dfrac{1}{2}\theta\left(2x+x^2\right)\\ &= \dfrac{1}{2}\theta x(2+x) \qquad (1)\end{aligned}$$
From (1):
$$(2+x)\theta=\dfrac{2A}{x}$$
Substituting into $P=(2+x)\theta+2x$:
$$\therefore\ P(x)=2x+\dfrac{2A}{x}$$','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Finds correct expressions for the perimeter and area, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds the correct expression for the perimeter or area, or equivalent merit',1628,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds correct expressions for the perimeter and area, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the correct expression for the perimeter or area, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Provides correct solution"], [2, "Finds correct expressions for the perimeter and area, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the correct expression for the perimeter or area, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
$$\begin{aligned} P'' &= 2-\dfrac{2A}{x^2}=0\\ x^2 &= A\\ x &= \sqrt{A} \quad (x>0)\end{aligned}$$
Testing the nature with the second derivative:
$$P''''=\dfrac{4A}{x^3}>0 \text{ when } x=\sqrt{A}$$
$\therefore$ This gives a minimum value.

Using (1) with $x=\sqrt{A}$:
$$A=\dfrac{1}{2}\theta\sqrt{A}\left(2+\sqrt{A}\right)$$
$$\theta=\dfrac{2A}{\sqrt{A}\left(2+\sqrt{A}\right)}=\dfrac{2\sqrt{A}}{2+\sqrt{A}}$$
Since $2+\sqrt{A}>\sqrt{A}$:
$$\begin{aligned} \theta &< \dfrac{2\sqrt{A}}{\sqrt{A}}\\ &= 2\end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ If $P(x)$ is minimised, $\theta<2$.','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Expresses $\theta$ in terms of $A$, or equivalent merit; 1: Shows $x=\sqrt{A}$ is a minimum, or equivalent merit',1628,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Expresses $\\theta$ in terms of $A$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Shows $x=\\sqrt{A}$ is a minimum, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Provides correct solution"], [2, "Expresses $\\theta$ in terms of $A$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Shows $x=\\sqrt{A}$ is a minimum, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
