$$2\pi r+3x=100$$
$$r=\dfrac{100-3x}{2\pi}$$
Area of circle $\pi r^2$; area of the equilateral triangle $\dfrac{1}{2}x^2\sin 60^\circ$:
$$\begin{aligned} A(x) &= \text{Area of circle}+\text{area of equilateral triangle} \\ &= \pi r^2+\dfrac{1}{2}x^2\sin 60^\circ \\ &= \pi r^2+\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{4}x^2 \\ &= \pi\left(\dfrac{100-3x}{2\pi}\right)^2+\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{4}x^2 \\ &= \dfrac{1}{4}\left(\sqrt{3}\,x^2+\dfrac{(100-3x)^2}{\pi}\right) \end{aligned}$$','2: Provides correct solution; 1: Finds an expression for $r$ in terms of $x$, or equivalent merit',1630,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds an expression for $r$ in terms of $x$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Provides correct solution"], [1, "Finds an expression for $r$ in terms of $x$, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');

