$$\begin{aligned}\mu&=\dfrac{1610}{35}\\&=46\end{aligned}$$
$2.5\%$ of orders leave within 10 days, and $2.5\%$ of a normal distribution lies below $z=-2$, so 10 days has a $z$-score of $-2$:
$$\begin{aligned}z&=\dfrac{x-\mu}{\sigma}\\-2&=\dfrac{10-46}{\sigma}\\-2\sigma&=-36\\\sigma&=18\end{aligned}$$
The discount goes to the $5\%$ of customers who wait longest, so we need the score corresponding to a $z$-score of $1.65$:
$$\begin{aligned}1.65&=\dfrac{x-46}{18}\\29.7&=x-46\\x&=75.7\end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ Customers who wait more than 76 days will receive a discount.','3: Correct solution; 2: Finds the mean and standard deviation; 1: Finds the mean',1356,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds the mean and standard deviation, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the mean, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Correct solution"], [2, "Finds the mean and standard deviation"], [1, "Finds the mean"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correct solution", "source_original": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Mean}&=\\dfrac{1610}{35}\\\\&=46\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince $2.5\\%$ of orders are despatched within 10 days, 10 has a $z$-score of $-2$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}z&=\\dfrac{\\bar{x}-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\\\-2&=\\dfrac{10-46}{\\sigma}\\\\-2\\sigma&=-36\\\\\\sigma&=18\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince the discount will be given to the $5\\%$ of customers who need to wait the longest, we need the score which correlates to a $z$-score of $1.65$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}1.65&=\\dfrac{x-46}{18}\\\\29.7&=x-46\\\\x&=75.7\\end{aligned}$$\n\nCustomers who wait more than 76 days will receive a discount.", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the $z$-score formula was written $z=\\dfrac{\\bar{x}-\\mu}{\\sigma}$; it is $z=\\dfrac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}$."}');
