$$\begin{aligned} A_1&=\int_{-2}^0\left(\dfrac{1}{2}x+3-(-x)\right)dx\\ &=\int_{-2}^0\left(\dfrac{3}{2}x+3\right)dx\\ &=\left[\dfrac{3x^2}{4}+3x\right]_{-2}^0\\ &=0-\left(\dfrac{3(-2)^2}{4}+3(-2)\right)\\ &=3 \end{aligned}$$
(Or as a triangle, $A_1=\dfrac{1}{2}\times 3\times 2=3$.)

So $7$ square units more are needed for $x$ from $0$ to $k$.

The whole triangle from $x=0$ to $x=6$ has area $\dfrac{1}{2}\times 3\times 6=9>7$, so $k<6$.

For $0\le x\le k$, the region lies between the line and $y=x$:
$$\begin{aligned} 7&=\int_0^k\left(\dfrac{1}{2}x+3-x\right)dx\\ 7&=\int_0^k\left(-\dfrac{1}{2}x+3\right)dx\\ 7&=\left[-\dfrac{1}{4}x^2+3x\right]_0^k\\ 7&=-\dfrac{1}{4}k^2+3k\\ k^2-12k+28&=0\\ (k-6)^2&=8\\ k&=6\pm 2\sqrt{2} \end{aligned}$$
But $k<6$:
$$\therefore\ k=6-2\sqrt{2}$$','4: Correct answer, $k=6-2\sqrt{2}$ only; 3: Obtains $k^2-12k+28=0$, or equivalent merit; 2: Sets up the integral for the remaining area of 7, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds the area of 3 between $x=-2$ and $x=0$, or equivalent merit',1370,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Obtains $k^2-12k+28=0$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Sets up the integral for the remaining area of 7, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the area of 3 between $x=-2$ and $x=0$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"concern": "transcribed from handwritten marking guidelines (scanned pages, no text layer)", "criteria_original": [[4, "Correct answer, $k=6-2\\sqrt{2}$ only"], [3, "Obtains $k^2-12k+28=0$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Sets up the integral for the remaining area of 7, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the area of 3 between $x=-2$ and $x=0$, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correct answer, $k=6-2\\sqrt{2}$ only"}');
