$$A_n=83\,000(1.005)^n-760\big((1.005)^{n-1}+(1.005)^{n-2}(1.1)+\cdots+(1.1)^{n-1}\big)$$
The bracket is a geometric series with first term $a=(1.005)^{n-1}$, common ratio $r=\dfrac{1.1}{1.005}$ and $n$ terms. Multiplying the top and bottom of $S_n=\dfrac{a(r^n-1)}{r-1}$ by $1.005$:
$$\begin{aligned} S_n&=\dfrac{(1.005)^{n-1}\left(\frac{(1.1)^n}{(1.005)^n}-1\right)}{\frac{1.1}{1.005}-1}\\ &=\dfrac{(1.1)^n-(1.005)^n}{1.1-1.005}\\ &=\dfrac{(1.1)^n-(1.005)^n}{0.095}\end{aligned}$$
So
$$\begin{aligned} A_n&=83\,000(1.005)^n-\dfrac{760}{0.095}\big((1.1)^n-(1.005)^n\big)\\ &=83\,000(1.005)^n-8000(1.1)^n+8000(1.005)^n\\ &=91\,000(1.005)^n-8000(1.1)^n\end{aligned}$$',NULL,1632,'claude-opus-5-5','gen-v2',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Sums the geometric series correctly, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Writes the general expression for $A_n$ with the geometric series, or equivalent merit"]]','{"confidence": 0.98, "check": "Closed form matches month-by-month simulation for n=1..26."}');
$$\begin{aligned} 91\,000(1.005)^n&\le8000(1.1)^n\\ \left(\dfrac{1.1}{1.005}\right)^n&\ge\dfrac{91}{8}\\ n&\ge\dfrac{\ln\left(\frac{91}{8}\right)}{\ln\left(\frac{1.1}{1.005}\right)}\approx26.9\end{aligned}$$
So $A_{26}>0$ and $A_{27}<0$: the final payment is the $27$th, and it is smaller than the scheduled $760(1.1)^{26}$.
