$$\begin{aligned} \text{LHS} &= \dfrac{1}{\cos x} + \dfrac{\sin x}{\cos x} \\ &= \dfrac{1 + \sin x}{\cos x} \\ &= \dfrac{(1 + \sin x)(1 - \sin x)}{\cos x\,(1 - \sin x)} \\ &= \dfrac{1 - \sin^2 x}{\cos x\,(1 - \sin x)} \\ &= \dfrac{\cos^2 x}{\cos x\,(1 - \sin x)} \\ &= \dfrac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} = \text{RHS} \end{aligned}$$','2: Correct proof; 1: Multiplies numerator and denominator by $1 - \sin x$, or equivalent merit',1357,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Multiplies numerator and denominator by $1 - \\sin x$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"concern": "transcribed from handwritten solutions copy (images, no text layer)", "criteria_original": [[2, "Correct proof"], [1, "Multiplies numerator and denominator by $1 - \\sin x$, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correct proof"}');
