$$f''''(4)=-6\times4+12=-12<0 \text{ (concave down)}$$
$\therefore$ $(4,31)$ is a maximum turning point.','1: dy/dx = 0 solved; 1: two stationary points calculated; 1: nature of points determined using either the slope test or concavity test',644,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Calculates the two stationary points, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Solves $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=0$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "dy/dx = 0 solved"], [1, "two stationary points calculated"], [1, "nature of points determined using either the slope test or concavity test"]], "top_criterion_original": "dy/dx = 0 solved", "source_original": "$f''''(4)=-4\\times4+12=-4<0$, concave down", "corrected": "Corrected from source: f''''(4) = -6 × 4 + 12 = -12 (source wrote -4 × 4 + 12 = -4); still < 0, so the conclusion is unchanged."}');
