Test the solutions in the original equation.

$x=-\dfrac{3}{7}$:
$$\left|2 \times \left(-\dfrac{3}{7}\right) - 3\right| = \dfrac{27}{7},\qquad 9 \times \left(-\dfrac{3}{7}\right)=-\dfrac{27}{7}$$
These are not equal, so $x = -\dfrac{3}{7}$ is not a solution.

$x=\dfrac{3}{11}$:
$$\left|2 \times \dfrac{3}{11} - 3\right| = \dfrac{27}{11},\qquad 9 \times \dfrac{3}{11}=\dfrac{27}{11}$$
These are equal.
$$\therefore\ x = \dfrac{3}{11}$$','3: Solves both equations and correctly tests solutions; 2: Solves two equations correctly; 1: Solves one equation correctly',1359,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Solves two equations correctly, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Solves one equation correctly, or equivalent merit"]]','{"concern": "transcribed from handwritten solutions copy (images, no text layer)", "criteria_original": [[3, "Solves both equations and correctly tests solutions"], [2, "Solves two equations correctly"], [1, "Solves one equation correctly"]], "top_criterion_original": "Solves both equations and correctly tests solutions"}');

