$$\begin{aligned} 12000 &= 3000n^{\frac{20}{10}} \\ n^2 &= 4 \\ n &= \pm 2 \end{aligned}$$
$n > 0$, so $n = 2$ and $P=3000\times 2^{\frac{t}{10}}$.

Using
$$\dfrac{d}{dt}\left(a^{kt}\right)=k\ln a\cdot a^{kt}$$
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{dP}{dt} &= 3000 \times \ln 2 \times \dfrac{1}{10} \times 2^{\frac{t}{10}} \\ &= 300\ln 2 \times 2^{\frac{t}{10}} \end{aligned}$$
Set $\dfrac{dP}{dt} = 6000$:
$$\begin{aligned} 6000 &= 300\ln 2 \times 2^{\frac{t}{10}} \\ 2^{\frac{t}{10}} &= \dfrac{20}{\ln 2} \\ \dfrac{t}{10} &= \log_2\left(\dfrac{20}{\ln 2}\right) \\ &= \log_2 20 - \log_2(\ln 2) \\ t &= 10\left(\dfrac{\ln 20}{\ln 2} - \dfrac{\ln(\ln 2)}{\ln 2}\right) \\ &\approx 48.5 \text{ days} \end{aligned}$$','4: Finds $n$, finds $\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, correctly substitutes 6000 into $\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, correctly calculates $t$; 3: 3 of the above (or 1 error); 2: 2 of the above (or 2 errors); 1: One of the above',1359,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Three of: finds $n$, finds $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, substitutes 6000 into $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, calculates $t$ (or 1 error), or equivalent merit"], [2, "Two of the above (or 2 errors), or equivalent merit"], [1, "One of the above, or equivalent merit"]]','{"concern": "transcribed from handwritten solutions copy (images, no text layer)", "criteria_original": [[4, "Finds $n$, finds $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, correctly substitutes 6000 into $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, correctly calculates $t$"], [3, "3 of the above (or 1 error)"], [2, "2 of the above (or 2 errors)"], [1, "One of the above"]], "top_criterion_original": "Finds $n$, finds $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, correctly substitutes 6000 into $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}$, correctly calculates $t$"}');
