$$\begin{aligned} v(t)&=3\sqrt{t+1}-9\\ &=3(t+1)^{\frac{1}{2}}-9\\ x(t)&=\int\left(3(t+1)^{\frac{1}{2}}-9\right)dt\\ &=\dfrac{3(t+1)^{\frac{3}{2}}}{\frac{3}{2}}-9t+C\\ &=2\sqrt{(t+1)^3}-9t+C\\ &=2(t+1)\sqrt{t+1}-9t+C \end{aligned}$$
The particle starts at $O$, so $x=0$ when $t=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} 0&=2(1)\sqrt{1}-9(0)+C\\ \therefore\ C&=-2 \end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\ x(t)=2(t+1)\sqrt{t+1}-9t-2 \text{ as required}$$','2: Provides correct solution with appropriate and logical steps shown; 1: Correctly integrates v(t) but does not evaluate the constant of integration or makes an error',1361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correctly integrates $v(t)$ but does not evaluate the constant of integration or makes an error, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Provides correct solution with appropriate and logical steps shown"], [1, "Correctly integrates v(t) but does not evaluate the constant of integration or makes an error"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution with appropriate and logical steps shown"}');
