By part (a), $y=2\tan x+\sec^2x$:
$$\begin{aligned} A&=\int_{-\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{6}}\left(2\tan x+\sec^2x\right)dx\\ &=\int_{-\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{6}}\left(\dfrac{2\sin x}{\cos x}+\sec^2x\right)dx\\ &=\Big[-2\ln|\cos x|+\tan x\Big]_{-\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{6}}\\ &=\left(-2\ln\left|\cos\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right|+\tan\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)-\left(-2\ln\left|\cos\left(-\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)\right|+\tan\left(-\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)\right)\\ &=-2\ln\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}-\left(-2\ln\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\right)\\ &=-2\ln\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}+2\ln\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\\ &=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{3}}\\ &=\dfrac{2\sqrt{3}}{3}\ \text{units}^2 \end{aligned}$$','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Correctly integrates but makes an error in evaluating; 1: Changes tan x into sin x/cos x before integrating',1361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correctly integrates but makes an error in evaluating, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Changes $\\tan x$ into $\\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$ before integrating, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Provides correct solution"], [2, "Correctly integrates but makes an error in evaluating"], [1, "Changes tan x into sin x/cos x before integrating"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
