$$\begin{aligned} \tan x&=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}\\ x&=\dfrac{\pi}{6},\ \dfrac{7\pi}{6} \end{aligned}$$
Between these points $y=\sqrt{3}\sin x$ is above $y=\cos x$:
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area}&=\int_{\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{7\pi}{6}}\left(\sqrt{3}\sin x-\cos x\right)dx\\ &=\Big[-\sqrt{3}\cos x-\sin x\Big]_{\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{7\pi}{6}}\\ &=\left(-\sqrt{3}\cos\left(\dfrac{7\pi}{6}\right)-\sin\left(\dfrac{7\pi}{6}\right)\right)-\left(-\sqrt{3}\cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)-\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)\right)\\ &=\left(\sqrt{3}\cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)+\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)\right)-\left(-\sqrt{3}\cos\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)-\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right)\right)\\ &=\left(\sqrt{3}\times\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}+\dfrac{1}{2}\right)-\left(-\sqrt{3}\times\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}-\dfrac{1}{2}\right)\\ &=\dfrac{3}{2}+\dfrac{1}{2}+\dfrac{3}{2}+\dfrac{1}{2}\\ &=\dfrac{8}{2}\\ &=4\ \text{units}^2 \end{aligned}$$','4: All prior steps completed, shows correct substitution leading to the correct solution; 3: Both prior steps completed, finds the correct primitive function; Allow 1: Forms an appropriate integral for finding the area; Allow 1: Solves the equation tan x = 1/sqrt(3) to find intersection points',1361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Finds the correct primitive function, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Solves $\\tan x=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ to find the intersection points and forms an appropriate integral for the area, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Solves $\\tan x=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ to find the intersection points or forms an appropriate integral for the area, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[4, "All prior steps completed, shows correct substitution leading to the correct solution"], [3, "Both prior steps completed, finds the correct primitive function; Allow 1: Forms an appropriate integral for finding the area; Allow 1: Solves the equation tan x = 1/sqrt(3) to find intersection points"]], "top_criterion_original": "All prior steps completed, shows correct substitution leading to the correct solution"}');
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{1}{2}\times\dfrac{4}{3}\pi r^3+\pi r^2h&=0.66\pi\\ \dfrac{2}{3}r^3+r^2h&=0.66\\ 2r^3+3r^2h&=\dfrac{99}{50}\\ 3r^2h&=\dfrac{99}{50}-2r^3\\ h&=\dfrac{33}{50r^2}-\dfrac{2r}{3} \end{aligned}$$
The metal is a hemispherical shell, the base circle and the curved side of the cylinder:
$$\begin{aligned} A&=\dfrac{1}{2}\times4\pi r^2+\pi r^2+2\pi rh\\ &=2\pi r^2+\pi r^2+2\pi rh\\ &=3\pi r^2+2\pi r\left(\dfrac{33}{50r^2}-\dfrac{2r}{3}\right)\\ &=3\pi r^2+\dfrac{33\pi}{25r}-\dfrac{4\pi r^2}{3}\\ &=\dfrac{33\pi}{25r}+\dfrac{5\pi r^2}{3}\ \text{as required} \end{aligned}$$','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Finds an equation for the surface area in terms of r (eliminating h); 1: Writes equation for volume incorporating the given volume.',1361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds an equation for the surface area in terms of $r$ (eliminating $h$), or equivalent merit"], [1, "Writes an equation for the volume incorporating the given volume, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Provides correct solution"], [2, "Finds an equation for the surface area in terms of r (eliminating h)"], [1, "Writes equation for volume incorporating the given volume."]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
Stationary points occur when $A''=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{10\pi r}{3}-\dfrac{33\pi}{25r^2}&=0\\ \dfrac{10\pi r^3}{3}-\dfrac{33\pi}{25}&=0\\ \dfrac{10\pi r^3}{3}&=\dfrac{33\pi}{25}\\ r^3&=\dfrac{99}{250}\\ \therefore\ r&=\sqrt[3]{\dfrac{99}{250}} \end{aligned}$$
Second derivative test:
$$\begin{aligned} A''''&=\dfrac{66\pi}{25}\left(\sqrt[3]{\dfrac{99}{250}}\right)^{-3}+\dfrac{10\pi}{3}\\ &=10\pi \end{aligned}$$
$A''''>0$, so $A$ is a minimum at $r=\sqrt[3]{\dfrac{99}{250}}$.

Using $h$ from part (a):
$$\begin{aligned} h&=\dfrac{33}{50r^2}-\dfrac{2r}{3}\\ &=\dfrac{99-100r^3}{150r^2}\\ &=\dfrac{99-100\left(\sqrt[3]{\frac{99}{250}}\right)^3}{150\left(\sqrt[3]{\frac{99}{250}}\right)^2}\\ &=\dfrac{99-100\left(\frac{99}{250}\right)}{150\left(\frac{99}{250}\right)^{\frac{2}{3}}}\\ &=\dfrac{99-\frac{990}{25}}{150}\times\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^{-\frac{2}{3}}\\ &=\dfrac{297}{750}\times\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^{-\frac{2}{3}}\\ &=\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^1\times\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^{-\frac{2}{3}}\\ &=\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^{\frac{1}{3}}\\ \therefore\ h&=\sqrt[3]{\dfrac{99}{250}} \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ The dimensions are $r=h=\sqrt[3]{\dfrac{99}{250}}$ m.

Alternative end of solution, from the volume equation in part (a):
$$\begin{aligned} 2r^3+3r^2h&=1.98\\ h&=\dfrac{1.98-2r^3}{3r^2}\\ &=\dfrac{1.98-2\left(\sqrt[3]{\frac{99}{250}}\right)^3}{3\left(\sqrt[3]{\frac{99}{250}}\right)^2}\\ &=\dfrac{1.98-\frac{99}{125}}{3}\times\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^{-\frac{2}{3}}\\ &=\dfrac{99}{250}\times\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^{-\frac{2}{3}}\\ &=\left(\dfrac{99}{250}\right)^{\frac{1}{3}}\\ \therefore\ h&=\sqrt[3]{\dfrac{99}{250}} \end{aligned}$$','4: Provides correct dimensions with relevant working including justification that the given r value gives a minimum SA; 3: Provides correct dimensions or justifies that the determined r value gives a minimum.; 2: Finds the value of r that makes A''=0; 1: Differentiates A with respect to r',1361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Provides correct dimensions or justifies that the determined $r$ value gives a minimum, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds the value of $r$ that makes $A''=0$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Differentiates $A$ with respect to $r$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[4, "Provides correct dimensions with relevant working including justification that the given r value gives a minimum SA"], [3, "Provides correct dimensions or justifies that the determined r value gives a minimum."], [2, "Finds the value of r that makes A''=0"], [1, "Differentiates A with respect to r"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct dimensions with relevant working including justification that the given r value gives a minimum SA", "source_original": "2r^3+3r^2h=0.66 (first line of the alternate end of solution)", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the alternate ending starts from 2r^3 + 3r^2h = 1.98 (three times the volume equation divided by pi), not 0.66; its next line already uses 1.98."}');

