Integrating to find the velocity:
$$v=\dfrac{8e^{-2t}}{-2}+\dfrac{3e^{-t}}{-1}+c$$
When $t=0$, $v=-6$:
$$\begin{aligned} -6&=-4e^0-3e^0+c\\ -6&=-7+c\\ c&=1 \end{aligned}$$
$$v=-4e^{-2t}-3e^{-t}+1$$
Integrating again:
$$x=\dfrac{-4e^{-2t}}{-2}-\dfrac{3e^{-t}}{-1}+t+k$$
When $t=0$, $x=5$:
$$\begin{aligned} 5&=2e^0+3e^0+0+k\\ 5&=5+k\\ k&=0 \end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} x&=2e^{-2t}+3e^{-t}+t\\ &=\dfrac{2}{e^{2t}}+\dfrac{3}{e^t}+t \end{aligned}$$','1: correct velocity; 1: correct displacement',1362,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds the correct velocity, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correct velocity"], [1, "correct displacement"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct velocity", "rubric_note": "Rewritten top-down from a one-mark-per-step rubric (owner rule, 11 Nov)."}');
$$\begin{aligned} 0&=-4e^{-2t}-3e^{-t}+1\\ 0&=4e^{-2t}+3e^{-t}-1\\ &=4(e^{-t})^2+3e^{-t}-1 \end{aligned}$$
Let $m=e^{-t}$:
$$\begin{aligned} 0&=4m^2+3m-1\\ &=(4m-1)(m+1)\\ m&=\dfrac{1}{4} \text{ or } m=-1 \end{aligned}$$
$e^{-t}=-1$ has no solution, since $e^{-t}>0$.
$$\begin{aligned} e^{-t}&=\dfrac{1}{4}\\ \ln e^{-t}&=\ln\dfrac{1}{4}\\ -t&=\ln 4^{-1}=-\ln 4\\ t&=\ln 4=1.386294361 \end{aligned}$$
When $t=\ln 4$:
$$\begin{aligned} x&=2e^{-2\ln 4}+3e^{-\ln 4}+\ln 4\\ &=2e^{\ln 4^{-2}}+3e^{\ln 4^{-1}}+\ln 4\\ &=2\times 4^{-2}+3\times 4^{-1}+\ln 4\\ &=\dfrac{2}{16}+\dfrac{3}{4}+\ln 4\\ &=\dfrac{7}{8}+\ln 4\\ &=2.261294361 \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ The particle is at rest when $t=\ln 4\approx 1.386$ seconds, at $x\approx 2.26$ m.','Marks not itemised on the copy (3 marks): quadratic in $e^{-t}$; $t=\ln 4$; $x=\dfrac{7}{8}+\ln 4\approx 2.26$ m',1362,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds $t=\\ln 4$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Forms the quadratic in $e^{-t}$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[null, "Marks not itemised on the copy (3 marks): quadratic in $e^{-t}$; $t=\\ln 4$; $x=\\dfrac{7}{8}+\\ln 4\\approx 2.26$ m"]], "top_criterion_original": "Marks not itemised on the copy (3 marks): quadratic in $e^{-t}$; $t=\\ln 4$; $x=\\dfrac{7}{8}+\\ln 4\\approx 2.26$ m", "rubric_note": "Source gives 3 marks without itemising them (quadratic in e^(-t); t = ln 4; x = 7/8 + ln 4); written top-down in that order."}');

