1 million unique views requires the sum of the geometric progression. Using $S_n=\dfrac{a(r^n-1)}{r-1}$:
$$\begin{aligned} 1000000&=\dfrac{8(5^n-1)}{4}\\ 1000000&=2(5^n-1)\\ 5^n-1&=500000\\ 5^n&=500001\\ n\ln 5&=\ln 500001\\ n&=\dfrac{\ln 500001}{\ln 5}\\ &=8.1533\ldots \end{aligned}$$
Therefore it takes 9 full days to reach 1 million unique views.','3: Correctly determines the number of days after solving the geometric progression equation using logarithm laws; 2: Correctly solves the required equation using logarithm laws or equivalent effort; 1: Identifies that a sum of a geometric progression is required and obtains the equation $1000000=\dfrac{8(5^n-1)}{4}$ or equivalent',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correctly solves the required equation using logarithm laws, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Identifies that a sum of a geometric progression is required and obtains the equation $1000000=\\dfrac{8(5^n-1)}{4}$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Correctly determines the number of days after solving the geometric progression equation using logarithm laws"], [2, "Correctly solves the required equation using logarithm laws or equivalent effort"], [1, "Identifies that a sum of a geometric progression is required and obtains the equation $1000000=\\dfrac{8(5^n-1)}{4}$ or equivalent"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correctly determines the number of days after solving the geometric progression equation using logarithm laws", "marker_note": "Many students used $T_n$ rather than $S_n$; 2 marks were awarded if $T_n$ was used. Coincidentally, using $T_n$ produces the same answer.", "source_original": "5^n&=5000001\\\\ n\\ln 5&=\\ln 5000001\\\\ n&=\\dfrac{\\ln 5000001}{\\ln 5}", "corrected": "Corrected from source: 5^n = 500 001 (from 5^n - 1 = 500 000), not 5 000 001; the value n = 8.1533... already uses 500 001."}');
