There is no chance of winning when the two dice show the same number or adjoining numbers:
$$\begin{aligned} P(\text{no chance})&=\dfrac{\text{number of pairs with no gap}}{\text{total possibilities}}\\ &=\dfrac{16}{36}\\ &=\dfrac{4}{9} \end{aligned}$$','2: correct solution; 1: correctly calculates probability for same number or adjoining numbers or equivalent',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correctly calculates the probability for the same number or adjoining numbers, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "correct solution"], [1, "correctly calculates probability for same number or adjoining numbers or equivalent"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct solution"}');
$$\begin{aligned} &8 \text{ combinations leave a gap for one winning number}\\ &6 \text{ combinations leave a gap for two winning numbers}\\ &4 \text{ combinations leave a gap for three winning numbers}\\ &2 \text{ combinations leave a gap for four winning numbers} \end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} \therefore\ P(\text{winning})&=\dfrac{1}{36}\left[8\times\dfrac{1}{6}+6\times\dfrac{2}{6}+4\times\dfrac{3}{6}+2\times\dfrac{4}{6}\right]\\ &=\dfrac{1}{36}\left(\dfrac{8}{6}+\dfrac{12}{6}+\dfrac{12}{6}+\dfrac{8}{6}\right)\\ &=\dfrac{1}{36}\left(\dfrac{40}{6}\right)\\ &=\dfrac{5}{27} \end{aligned}$$','2: correct solution; 1: correct solution with a minor error or correct answer with insufficient explanation to justify validity of method',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correct solution with a minor error, or correct answer with insufficient explanation to justify the validity of the method, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "correct solution"], [1, "correct solution with a minor error or correct answer with insufficient explanation to justify validity of method"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct solution", "marker_note": "It is important to provide reasoning for your calculations, so that marks can be awarded."}');
$$\begin{aligned} \cos A&=\dfrac{3^2+5^2-6^2}{2(3)(5)}\\ &=\dfrac{-1}{15}\\ \angle A&=\cos^{-1}\left(\dfrac{-1}{15}\right)\\ &=93.8^\circ\\ &=94^\circ\ \text{(nearest degree)} \end{aligned}$$','2: Correctly applies the Cosine rule; correct final rounded answer; 1: Shows partial correct working towards finding an unknown angle',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Shows partial correct working towards finding an unknown angle, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Correctly applies the Cosine rule; correct final rounded answer"], [1, "Shows partial correct working towards finding an unknown angle"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correctly applies the Cosine rule; correct final rounded answer"}');
