$$\begin{aligned} \text{LHS}&=\tan\theta\sin\theta+\cos\theta\\ &=\dfrac{\sin\theta}{\cos\theta}\sin\theta+\cos\theta\\ &=\dfrac{\sin^2\theta}{\cos\theta}+\dfrac{\cos^2\theta}{\cos\theta}\\ &=\dfrac{1}{\cos\theta}\\ &=\sec\theta=\text{RHS} \end{aligned}$$','2: Correctly applies trigonometric identities to prove LHS=RHS; 1: Shows partial correct working towards proving LHS=RHS',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Shows partial correct working towards proving LHS $=$ RHS, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Correctly applies trigonometric identities to prove LHS=RHS"], [1, "Shows partial correct working towards proving LHS=RHS"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correctly applies trigonometric identities to prove LHS=RHS"}');
