$$\begin{aligned} 2\sin^2x-3\sin x-2&=0\\ 2u^2-3u-2&=0\\ 2u^2-4u+u-2&=0\\ 2u(u-2)+1(u-2)&=0\\ (2u+1)(u-2)&=0\\ u&=-\dfrac{1}{2} \text{ or } u=2 \end{aligned}$$
$\sin x=2$ has no solution, since $-1\le\sin x\le1$.

$\therefore\sin x=-\dfrac{1}{2}$. $\sin x$ is negative in the 3rd and 4th quadrants, and the related angle is $\dfrac{\pi}{6}$:
$$\begin{aligned} x&=\pi+\dfrac{\pi}{6},\ 2\pi-\dfrac{\pi}{6}\\ \therefore\ x&=\dfrac{7\pi}{6},\ \dfrac{11\pi}{6} \end{aligned}$$','3: Correctly shows all the following: factorising a quadratic; determining two solutions for $\sin x$ and eliminating one; solving appropriately and determining the two correct values of $x$; 2: Contains partially correct working but omits at least one of the above points; 1: Contains partially accurate working but omits at least two of the points listed above',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Omits one of: factorising the quadratic; determining two solutions for $\\sin x$ and eliminating one; solving for the two correct values of $x$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Omits two of these steps, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Correctly shows all the following: factorising a quadratic; determining two solutions for $\\sin x$ and eliminating one; solving appropriately and determining the two correct values of $x$"], [2, "Contains partially correct working but omits at least one of the above points"], [1, "Contains partially accurate working but omits at least two of the points listed above"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correctly shows all the following: factorising a quadratic; determining two solutions for $\\sin x$ and eliminating one; solving appropriately and determining the two correct values of $x$"}');
$$\text{Perimeter}=r+r\theta+\dfrac{\pi r}{2}$$','1: Correct expression for the perimeter',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "Correct expression for the perimeter"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correct expression for the perimeter"}');
$$\begin{aligned} 1&=\dfrac{1}{2}r^2\theta+\dfrac{1}{2}\pi\left(\dfrac{r}{2}\right)^2\\ 1&=\dfrac{1}{2}r^2\theta+\dfrac{1}{2}\pi\dfrac{r^2}{4}\\ 1&=\dfrac{1}{2}r^2\theta+\dfrac{1}{8}\pi r^2\\ \dfrac{1}{2}r^2\theta&=1-\dfrac{1}{8}\pi r^2\\ r^2\theta&=2-\dfrac{1}{4}\pi r^2\\ \theta&=\dfrac{2}{r^2}-\dfrac{\pi r^2}{4r^2}\\ \theta&=\dfrac{8}{4r^2}-\dfrac{\pi r^2}{4r^2}\\ \therefore\ \theta&=\dfrac{8-\pi r^2}{4r^2} \end{aligned}$$','2: Contains complete and correct working; 1: Contains partially accurate working showing the correct formula for one of the areas',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Contains partially accurate working showing the correct formula for one of the areas, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Contains complete and correct working"], [1, "Contains partially accurate working showing the correct formula for one of the areas"]], "top_criterion_original": "Contains complete and correct working"}');
