$$\begin{aligned} f''(x)&=\lim_{h\to0}\dfrac{x^2+2xh+h^2-x-h-(x^2-x)}{h}\\ &=\lim_{h\to0}\dfrac{2xh+h^2-h}{h}\\ &=\lim_{h\to0}\dfrac{h(2x+h-1)}{h}\\ &=\lim_{h\to0}(2x+h-1)\\ &=2x+0-1\\ &=2x-1 \end{aligned}$$','2: Applies the first principles rule to communicate the solution to the gradient function in a cohesive and clear manner; 1: Applies the result from part (a) and substituting it into the first principles formula OR makes some progress towards the correct solution. Must use first principles. Obtaining the correct derivative by the power rule will yield zero marks.',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Applies the result from part (a) and substitutes it into the first principles formula OR makes some progress towards the correct solution, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Applies the first principles rule to communicate the solution to the gradient function in a cohesive and clear manner"], [1, "Applies the result from part (a) and substituting it into the first principles formula OR makes some progress towards the correct solution. Must use first principles. Obtaining the correct derivative by the power rule will yield zero marks."]], "top_criterion_original": "Applies the first principles rule to communicate the solution to the gradient function in a cohesive and clear manner", "marker_note": "Must use first principles. Obtaining the correct derivative by the power rule will yield zero marks."}');
The gradient of the tangent at $x=-2$:
$$\begin{aligned} y''&=3(-2)^2-3\\ &=9 \end{aligned}$$
Using $y-y_1=m(x-x_1)$ at $(-2,0)$:
$$\begin{aligned} y-0&=9(x+2)\\ y&=9x+18 \end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\ m=9,\ b=18$$','3: Correctly finds the equation of the tangent and obtains the values of $m$ and $b$; 2: Correctly differentiates the function and obtains either ONE of $m$ OR $b$ OR makes significant progress towards the correct solution; 1: Correctly differentiates the function OR makes some progress towards the correct solution',1364,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correctly differentiates the function and obtains either ONE of $m$ OR $b$, OR makes significant progress towards the correct solution, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly differentiates the function OR makes some progress towards the correct solution, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Correctly finds the equation of the tangent and obtains the values of $m$ and $b$"], [2, "Correctly differentiates the function and obtains either ONE of $m$ OR $b$ OR makes significant progress towards the correct solution"], [1, "Correctly differentiates the function OR makes some progress towards the correct solution"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correctly finds the equation of the tangent and obtains the values of $m$ and $b$"}');

