A point $(x,y)$ on $y=f(x)$ moves to $\left(\dfrac{x-1}{2},y\right)$.

The minimum at $(2,1)$ moves to $\left(\dfrac{1}{2},1\right)$ and the horizontal point of inflection at $(-1,1)$ stays at $(-1,1)$.

