$$\begin{aligned}\int_1^7(\ln x+1)\,dx&=\int_1^7\dfrac{d}{dx}(x\ln x)\,dx\\ \int_1^7\ln x\,dx+\int_1^7dx&=\Big[x\ln x\Big]_1^7\\ \int_1^7\ln x\,dx&=\Big[x\ln x\Big]_1^7-\Big[x\Big]_1^7\\ &=7\ln 7-0-(7-1)\\ &=7\ln 7-6\end{aligned}$$','1: integrating both sides of equation in part (b) or equivalent merit; 2: correct integration or equivalent merit; 3: correct answer',1367,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correct integration, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Integrates both sides of the equation in part (b), or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "integrating both sides of equation in part (b) or equivalent merit"], [2, "correct integration or equivalent merit"], [3, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');
