$$\begin{aligned}\dot{x}&=\int 4\sin 2t\,dt\\ &=-2\cos 2t+C\end{aligned}$$
Initially the particle moves left at $1$ m/s, so $\dot{x}=-1$ when $t=0$:
$$\begin{aligned}-1&=-2\cos 0+C\\ C&=1\end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\dot{x}=1-2\cos 2t$$','1: integration of acceleration or equivalent merit; 2: correct answer',1367,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Integrates the acceleration, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "integration of acceleration or equivalent merit"], [2, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');
$$\begin{aligned}1-2\cos 2t&=0\\ \cos 2t&=\dfrac{1}{2}\\ 2t&=\dfrac{\pi}{3}\quad(\text{smallest positive solution})\\ t&=\dfrac{\pi}{6}\text{ seconds}\end{aligned}$$','1: finding $\cos 2t$ or equivalent merit; 2: correct answer',1367,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds $\\cos 2t$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "finding $\\cos 2t$ or equivalent merit"], [2, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');

The particle moves left until it stops at $t=\dfrac{\pi}{6}$, then moves right, so split the distance there:
$$\begin{aligned}d&=\left|\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{6}}(1-2\cos 2t)\,dt\right|+\int_{\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}(1-2\cos 2t)\,dt\\ &=\left|\Big[t-\sin 2t\Big]_0^{\frac{\pi}{6}}\right|+\Big[t-\sin 2t\Big]_{\frac{\pi}{6}}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}\\ &=\left|\dfrac{\pi}{6}-\sin\dfrac{\pi}{3}-0\right|+\dfrac{\pi}{2}-\sin\pi-\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}-\sin\dfrac{\pi}{3}\right)\\ &=\left|\dfrac{\pi}{6}-\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right|+\dfrac{\pi}{2}-\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}-\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)\\ &=\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}-\dfrac{\pi}{6}+\dfrac{\pi}{2}-\dfrac{\pi}{6}+\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\\ &=\sqrt{3}+\dfrac{\pi}{6}\text{ metres}\end{aligned}$$','1: expression of distance or equivalent merit; 2: correct integration or equivalent merit; 3: correct answer',1367,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correct integration, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correct expression for the distance, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "expression of distance or equivalent merit"], [2, "correct integration or equivalent merit"], [3, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');
$$\begin{aligned}\tan\theta&=\dfrac{QR}{x}\\ QR&=2x\end{aligned}$$
$PS=QR=2x$ (opposite sides of the rectangle). Applying Pythagoras'' theorem in right-angled triangle $POS$ (hypotenuse $OP=5$, the radius):
$$\begin{aligned}(x+y)^2+PS^2&=OP^2\\ (x+y)^2+(2x)^2&=5^2\\ (x+y)^2&=25-4x^2\end{aligned}$$
Since $x+y>0$:
$$\begin{aligned}x+y&=\sqrt{25-4x^2}\\ y&=-x+\sqrt{25-4x^2}\end{aligned}$$
The perimeter is $2QR+2RS$:
$$\begin{aligned}P&=2(2x)+2\left(-x+\sqrt{25-4x^2}\right)\\ &=2x+2\sqrt{25-4x^2}\end{aligned}$$','1: finding $QR$ or equivalent merit; 2: finding $y$ or equivalent merit; 3: correct answer',1367,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds $y$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds $QR$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "finding $QR$ or equivalent merit"], [2, "finding $y$ or equivalent merit"], [3, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');
$$\begin{aligned}P&=2x+2\left(25-4x^2\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}\\ \dfrac{dP}{dx}&=2+2\times\dfrac{1}{2}\left(25-4x^2\right)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\times(-8x)\\ &=2-\dfrac{8x}{\sqrt{25-4x^2}}\end{aligned}$$
Stationary points occur where $\dfrac{dP}{dx}=0$:
$$\begin{aligned}2-\dfrac{8x}{\sqrt{25-4x^2}}&=0\\ \dfrac{8x}{\sqrt{25-4x^2}}&=2\\ 4x&=\sqrt{25-4x^2}\\ 16x^2&=25-4x^2\\ 20x^2&=25\\ x^2&=\dfrac{5}{4}\\ x&=\dfrac{\sqrt{5}}{2}\quad(x>0)\end{aligned}$$
\extable{Ts1411_1}

$\therefore$ the maximum is at $x=\dfrac{\sqrt{5}}{2}$.
$$\begin{aligned}P&=2\times\dfrac{\sqrt{5}}{2}+2\sqrt{25-4\left(\dfrac{\sqrt{5}}{2}\right)^2}\\ &=\sqrt{5}+2\sqrt{20}\\ &=5\sqrt{5}\text{ metres}\end{aligned}$$','1: finding $\dfrac{dP}{dx}$ or equivalent merit; 2: finding $x$ or equivalent merit; 3: showing maximum at $x$ or equivalent merit; 4: correct answer',1367,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Shows the maximum at this $x$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds $x$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds $\\dfrac{dP}{dx}$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"concern": "Guide''s sign table gives dP/dx = 0.25 at x = 1; actual value is 2 − 8/√21 ≈ 0.254 (rounded); transcribed as printed", "criteria_original": [[1, "finding $\\dfrac{dP}{dx}$ or equivalent merit"], [2, "finding $x$ or equivalent merit"], [3, "showing maximum at $x$ or equivalent merit"], [4, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');

