$$\begin{aligned}&\int\dfrac{x^2-3x+4}{\sqrt{x}}\,dx\\&=\int\dfrac{x^2}{x^{\frac{1}{2}}}-\dfrac{3x}{x^{\frac{1}{2}}}+\dfrac{4}{x^{\frac{1}{2}}}\,dx\\&=\int x^{\frac{3}{2}}-3x^{\frac{1}{2}}+4x^{-\frac{1}{2}}\,dx\\&=\dfrac{x^{\frac{5}{2}}}{\frac{5}{2}}-\dfrac{3x^{\frac{3}{2}}}{\frac{3}{2}}+\dfrac{4x^{\frac{1}{2}}}{\frac{1}{2}}+C\\&=\dfrac{2x^{\frac{5}{2}}}{5}-2x^{\frac{3}{2}}+8x^{\frac{1}{2}}+C\end{aligned}$$','1: correct simplification using index laws; 1: correct antiderivative (including $+C$). $\frac{1}{2}$ mark deducted only once across Booklet 1 for leaving out the constant of integration. Marker: poorly attempted across the whole cohort; simplify first before integrating.',1371,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correct simplification using index laws, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correct simplification using index laws"], [1, "correct antiderivative (including $+C$). $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ mark deducted only once across Booklet 1 for leaving out the constant of integration. Marker: poorly attempted across the whole cohort; simplify first before integrating."]], "top_criterion_original": "correct simplification using index laws", "marker_note": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$ mark deducted only once across Booklet 1 for leaving out the constant of integration. Poorly attempted across the whole cohort; simplify first before integrating."}');
