$$B(t)=-k\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi t}{28}\right)+c$$
so $c$ is the centre and $k$ is the amplitude.

The centre is midway between the greatest and smallest heights:
$$c=\dfrac{28+4}{2}=16$$
The amplitude is the distance from the centre to the greatest height:
$$k=28-16=12$$
$$\therefore c=16,\ k=12$$','1: $c=16$; 1: $k=12$. $\frac{1}{2}$ mark deducted if $k=-12$; 1 mark deducted if values of $k$ and $c$ are switched. Marker: many students struggled with this question.',1371,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds $c=16$ or $k=12$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "$c=16$"], [1, "$k=12$. $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ mark deducted if $k=-12$; 1 mark deducted if values of $k$ and $c$ are switched. Marker: many students struggled with this question."]], "top_criterion_original": "$c=16$", "marker_note": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$ mark deducted if $k=-12$; 1 mark deducted if the values of $k$ and $c$ are switched. Many students struggled with this question."}');
