$$\begin{aligned}&\int_4^{e+3}\dfrac{x+7}{x-3}\,dx\\&=\int_4^{e+3}1+\dfrac{10}{x-3}\,dx\\&=\Big[x+10\ln|x-3|\Big]_4^{e+3}\\&=e+3+10\ln|e+3-3|-\big[4+10\ln|4-3|\big]\\&=e+3+10\ln e-\big[4+10\ln1\big]\\&=e+3+10-(4+0)\\&=e+3+10-4\\&=e+9\end{aligned}$$','1: correct integration and notation; 1: correct answer. $1\frac{1}{2}$ marks for $e-1+10=e-9$ (be careful: $-1+10=+9$); 1 mark for $e+3-4$ or equivalent merit; no marks if no integration was shown.',1371,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correct integration and notation, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correct integration and notation"], [1, "correct answer. $1\\dfrac{1}{2}$ marks for $e-1+10=e-9$ (be careful: $-1+10=+9$); 1 mark for $e+3-4$ or equivalent merit; no marks if no integration was shown."]], "top_criterion_original": "correct integration and notation", "marker_note": "$1\\dfrac{1}{2}$ marks for $e-1+10=e-9$ (be careful: $-1+10=+9$); 1 mark for $e+3-4$ or equivalent merit; no marks if no integration was shown."}');

Using $T_n=ar^{n-1}$ to find the number of terms:
$$\begin{aligned}2\times3^{n-1}&=39\,366\\3^{n-1}&=19\,683\\3^{n-1}&=3^9\\\therefore n-1&=9\\n&=10\end{aligned}$$
Or: $n-1=\log_3 19\,683=9$, so $n=10$.

