$$\begin{aligned}\dfrac{x-8}{6-x}&=\dfrac{x+4}{x-8}\\(x-8)^2&=(6-x)(x+4)\\x^2-16x+64&=6x+24-x^2-4x\\x^2-16x+64&=-x^2+2x+24\\2x^2-18x+40&=0\\2(x^2-9x+20)&=0\\2(x-4)(x-5)&=0\\\therefore x&=4\text{ or }5\end{aligned}$$
When $x=4$:
$$r=\dfrac{4-8}{6-4}=-2$$
When $x=5$:
$$r=\dfrac{5-8}{6-5}=-3$$
$\therefore$ the possible common ratios are $-2$ and $-3$.','1: equating ratios $\dfrac{x-8}{6-x}=\dfrac{x+4}{x-8}$; 1: $x=4$ or $5$; 1: both common ratios (CFPE allowed). Only $\frac{1}{2}$ of the last mark was awarded if $r$ was worked out but it was concluded that $r=4$ or $5$.',1371,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds $x=4$ or $5$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Equates the ratios $\\dfrac{x-8}{6-x}=\\dfrac{x+4}{x-8}$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "equating ratios $\\dfrac{x-8}{6-x}=\\dfrac{x+4}{x-8}$"], [1, "$x=4$ or $5$"], [1, "both common ratios (CFPE allowed). Only $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ of the last mark was awarded if $r$ was worked out but it was concluded that $r=4$ or $5$."]], "top_criterion_original": "equating ratios $\\dfrac{x-8}{6-x}=\\dfrac{x+4}{x-8}$", "marker_note": "CFPE allowed for the common ratios. Only $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ of the last mark was awarded if $r$ was worked out but it was concluded that $r=4$ or $5$."}');

