Method 1:
$$\begin{aligned}&\int_0^4\left(2+\dfrac{t}{t^2+1}\right)dt\\&=\left[2t+\dfrac{1}{2}\ln|t^2+1|\right]_0^4\\&=8+\dfrac{1}{2}\ln17\end{aligned}$$
Method 2:
$$\begin{aligned}x&=\int\left(2+\dfrac{t}{t^2+1}\right)dt\\&=2t+\dfrac{1}{2}\ln|t^2+1|+C\end{aligned}$$
At $t=0$, $x=C$.

At $t=4$, $x=8+\dfrac{1}{2}\ln17+C$.

$\therefore$ the change in displacement is $8+\dfrac{1}{2}\ln17$ metres.','0.5: integral; 0.5: boundaries (or $x$ at $t=0$); 0.5: primitive; 0.5: answer. Marker: many assumed $C=0$ (initial displacement 0), which cannot be assumed but was not penalised; some evaluated average velocity $\frac{\Delta x}{\Delta t}$ when the question asked for $\Delta x$; use $dt$ instead of $dx$; $d$ is not displacement.',1371,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Writes the integral with the correct boundaries, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[null, "0.5: integral; 0.5: boundaries (or $x$ at $t=0$); 0.5: primitive; 0.5: answer. Marker: many assumed $C=0$ (initial displacement 0), which cannot be assumed but was not penalised; some evaluated average velocity $\\dfrac{\\Delta x}{\\Delta t}$ when the question asked for $\\Delta x$; use $dt$ instead of $dx$; $d$ is not displacement."]], "top_criterion_original": "0.5: integral; 0.5: boundaries (or $x$ at $t=0$); 0.5: primitive; 0.5: answer. Marker: many assumed $C=0$ (initial displacement 0), which cannot be assumed but was not penalised; some evaluated average velocity $\\dfrac{\\Delta x}{\\Delta t}$ when the question asked for $\\Delta x$; use $dt$ instead of $dx$; $d$ is not displacement.", "marker_note": "Marked in half marks: $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for the integral, $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for the boundaries (or $x$ at $t=0$), $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for the primitive, $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for the answer. Many assumed $C=0$ (initial displacement 0), which cannot be assumed but was not penalised; some evaluated the average velocity $\\dfrac{\\Delta x}{\\Delta t}$ when the question asked for $\\Delta x$; use $dt$ instead of $dx$; $d$ is not displacement."}');
$$\begin{aligned}u&=t & v&=t^2+1\\u''&=1 & v''&=2t\end{aligned}$$
