$$\begin{aligned}a&=\dfrac{1-5^2}{(5^2+1)^2}\\&=-\dfrac{6}{169}\text{ ms}^{-2}\end{aligned}$$','1: quotient rule; 1: evaluation. 0.5 deducted for subsequent minor errors such as incorrect simplification. Marker: revise the quotient rule; many forgot to square the denominator; some used $uv''-vu''$ as the numerator.',1371,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correctly applies the quotient rule, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "quotient rule"], [1, "evaluation. 0.5 deducted for subsequent minor errors such as incorrect simplification. Marker: revise the quotient rule; many forgot to square the denominator; some used $uv''-vu''$ as the numerator."]], "top_criterion_original": "quotient rule", "source_original": "$\\dfrac{t^2+1-2t}{(t^2+1)^2}$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the quotient-rule numerator read t² + 1 − 2t; it is t² + 1 − 2t² (= 1 − t², as in the next line). Answer −6/169 unchanged.", "marker_note": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$ deducted for subsequent minor errors such as incorrect simplification. Revise the quotient rule; many forgot to square the denominator; some used $uv''-vu''$ as the numerator."}');
