Let the curve cross the $x$-axis at $x=b$.
$$\begin{aligned}\int_0^3 f(x)\,dx&=\int_0^b f(x)\,dx+\int_b^3 f(x)\,dx\\4&=-3+\int_b^3 f(x)\,dx\\\therefore\int_b^3 f(x)\,dx&=7\end{aligned}$$
Area of the rectangle $=6\times3=18$

$\therefore$ remaining area of the rectangle $=18-7=11$

$\therefore$ area next to the $y$-axis $=11+3=14$','1: Correct answer',1372,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"source_original": "$\\therefore\\ 3=-4+\\int_b^3 f(x)\\,dx$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the source wrote 3 = -4 + ∫_b^3 f(x) dx (values swapped); since ∫_0^3 f = 4 and area A = 3 this is 4 = -3 + ∫_b^3 f(x) dx. Result 7 unchanged."}');
