$$4\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi}{4}\times50\right)=4$$
The period of the sine function is $\dfrac{2\pi}{n}=8$, where $n=\dfrac{\pi}{4}$.

From $x=8$ to $x=48$, there are 5 complete cycles, in each of which the sine curve meets $y=\ln x$ twice.

From $x=0$ to $x=8$, and from $x=48$ to $x=50$, there is only one intersection each.

So there are $5\times2+1+1=12$ intersections.','1: Correct answer',1372,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{}');

