$$6.38774\times\$15\,000=\$95\,816.10$$
This amount continues to earn interest for the remaining 9 years at 2.50% per annum, so it is multiplied by $1.025^9$.

Similarly, the four \$20 000 deposits (end of years 7 to 10) are worth $4.15252\times\$20\,000$ at the end of year 10, and earn interest for 5 more years:
$$4.15252\times\$20\,000\times1.025^5$$
Thus the final account balance at the end of 15 years is:
$$\begin{aligned}&6.38774\times\$15\,000\times1.025^9+4.15252\times\$20\,000\times1.025^5\\&=\$213\,625.08\text{ (nearest cent)}\end{aligned}$$
Alternate method (in stages, rounding to the nearest cent):
$$\begin{aligned}\text{End of 6 years: }&6.38774\times\$15\,000=\$95\,816.10\\\text{End of 10 years: }&4.15252\times\$20\,000+\$95\,816.10\times1.025^4=\$188\,813.45\\\text{End of 15 years: }&\$188\,813.45\times1.025^5=\$213\,625.09\end{aligned}$$
Depending on how the stages are rounded, the final result differs by a few cents.','4: Correct answer with sufficient reasoning; 3: Applies the interest rate in the years after deposits have stopped, or equivalent merit; 2: Takes the appropriate products of deposit amount and future value, or equivalent merit; 1: Identifies the appropriate values in the table',1372,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Applies the interest rate in the years after deposits have stopped, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Takes the appropriate products of deposit amount and future value, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Identifies the appropriate values in the table, or equivalent merit"]]','{"source_original": "$6.38774\\times\\$15\\,000\\times 1.025^9+4.15252\\times\\$20\\,000\\times 1.025^5=\\$215\\,974.18$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the main method''s final value $215 974.18 does not match its own expression, which evaluates to $213 625.08 (agreeing with the source''s alternate method, $213 625.09).", "criteria_original": [[4, "Correct answer with sufficient reasoning"], [3, "Applies the interest rate in the years after deposits have stopped, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Takes the appropriate products of deposit amount and future value, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Identifies the appropriate values in the table"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correct answer with sufficient reasoning", "marker_note": "Correct answer with sufficient reasoning is required for full marks."}');

