At $B$, $BA$ makes $180^\circ-156^\circ=24^\circ$ with the north line (co-interior angles), and $BC$ is on a bearing of $123^\circ$:
$$\angle ABC=24^\circ+123^\circ=147^\circ$$
Using the cosine rule in $\triangle ABC$:
$$\begin{aligned}AC^2&=12^2+16^2-2\times 12\times 16\cos 147^\circ\\&=722.049\ldots\\AC&=26.8\ldots\\&\approx 27\text{ km}\end{aligned}$$','1: cosine rule with angle 147 degrees; 1: AC = 27 km. Comment: generally well done.',1373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Uses the cosine rule with angle $147^\\circ$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "cosine rule with angle 147 degrees"], [1, "AC = 27 km. Comment: generally well done."]], "top_criterion_original": "AC = 27 km. Comment: generally well done.", "marker_note": "Generally well done."}');
$$\begin{aligned}\dfrac{\sin\alpha}{12}&=\dfrac{\sin 147^\circ}{27}\\\alpha&=14.008\ldots^\circ\end{aligned}$$
$CB$ is on a bearing of $123^\circ+180^\circ=303^\circ$, which is $57^\circ$ west of north, and $CA$ is $\alpha$ closer to north:
$$\begin{aligned}\theta&=57^\circ-\alpha\\&=42.9917\ldots^\circ\end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned}\text{Required bearing}&=360^\circ-\theta\\&\approx 317^\circ\text{T}\end{aligned}$$','1: finding angle ACB using the sine rule; 1: correct bearing 317 degrees T. Comment: students with a clear diagram were generally more successful.',1373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds $\\angle ACB$ using the sine rule, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "finding angle ACB using the sine rule"], [1, "correct bearing 317 degrees T. Comment: students with a clear diagram were generally more successful."]], "top_criterion_original": "correct bearing 317 degrees T. Comment: students with a clear diagram were generally more successful.", "marker_note": "Students with a clear diagram were generally more successful."}');
