The curve meets the $x$-axis where $2\sqrt{x-1}=0$, so $x=1$.

When $x=10$, $y=2\sqrt{9}=6$.

The shaded area is the $10\times 6$ rectangle minus the area under the curve from $x=1$ to $x=10$:
$$\text{Area of rectangle}=10\times 6=60$$
$$\begin{aligned}A&=60-2\int_1^{10}\sqrt{x-1}\,dx\\&=60-2\int_1^{10}(x-1)^{\frac{1}{2}}\,dx\\&=60-2\left[\dfrac{2}{3}(x-1)^{\frac{3}{2}}\right]_1^{10}\\&=60-\dfrac{4}{3}(27-0)\\&=24\text{ u}^2\end{aligned}$$
Alternative solution: write $x$ as a function of $y$ and integrate along the $y$-axis:
$$\begin{aligned}\dfrac{y}{2}&=\sqrt{x-1}\\x-1&=\dfrac{y^2}{4}\\x&=\dfrac{y^2}{4}+1\end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned}A&=\int_0^6\left(\dfrac{y^2}{4}+1\right)dy\\&=\left[\dfrac{y^3}{12}+y\right]_0^6\\&=24\text{ u}^2\end{aligned}$$','1: correct area expression (rectangle minus integral, or x as a function of y); 1: correct primitive; 1: correct answer. This question was very well done.',1373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correct primitive, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correct area expression (rectangle minus integral, or $x$ as a function of $y$), or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correct area expression (rectangle minus integral, or x as a function of y)"], [1, "correct primitive"], [1, "correct answer. This question was very well done."]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer. This question was very well done.", "marker_note": "This question was very well done."}');
