$$\begin{aligned}f''(x)&=5\cos(5x)-5x\times 5\sin(5x)\\&=5\cos(5x)-25x\sin(5x)\end{aligned}$$','1: Provide correct answer.',1373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "Provide correct answer."]], "top_criterion_original": "Provide correct answer.", "source_original": "$$\\begin{aligned}f''(x)&=5\\cos(5x)-5x\\times 5\\sin(5x)\\\\&=5\\cos(5x)-25\\sin(5x)\\end{aligned}$$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the last line printed $5\\cos(5x)-25\\sin(5x)$, missing the factor $x$; it is $5\\cos(5x)-25x\\sin(5x)$ (as used in part (ii))."}');
$$\begin{aligned}f''(x)&=5\cos(5x)-25x\sin(5x)\\25x\sin(5x)&=5\cos(5x)-f''(x)\\x\sin(5x)&=\dfrac{1}{25}\big(5\cos(5x)-f''(x)\big)\end{aligned}$$
Integrating both sides, with $\displaystyle\int f''(x)\,dx=f(x)=5x\cos(5x)$:
$$\begin{aligned}\int x\sin(5x)\,dx&=\dfrac{1}{25}\int\big(5\cos(5x)-f''(x)\big)\,dx\\&=\dfrac{1}{25}\big(\sin(5x)-f(x)\big)+C\\&=\dfrac{\sin(5x)-5x\cos(5x)}{25}+C\end{aligned}$$','3: Correctly evaluate the indefinite integral; 2: Make progress with correct integrand; 1: Correctly express $x\sin(5x)$ using the derivative from part (i). Comments: answered generally well; some students were confused with the coefficient of $x\sin(5x)$; a few students forgot the constant term.',1373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Makes progress with correct integrand, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly expresses $x\\sin(5x)$ using the derivative from part (i), or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Correctly evaluate the indefinite integral"], [2, "Make progress with correct integrand"], [1, "Correctly express $x\\sin(5x)$ using the derivative from part (i). Comments: answered generally well; some students were confused with the coefficient of $x\\sin(5x)$; a few students forgot the constant term."]], "top_criterion_original": "Correctly evaluate the indefinite integral", "marker_note": "Answered generally well; some students were confused with the coefficient of $x\\sin(5x)$; a few students forgot the constant term.", "source_original": "$\\ldots=\\dfrac{\\sin(5x)-5x\\cos(x)}{25}+C$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the final line printed $5x\\cos(x)$; it is $5x\\cos(5x)$."}');

