Writing $g(x)$ in vertex form:
$$\begin{aligned}g(x)&=\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\big((-x+2)-3\big)^2-1\right)\\&=\dfrac{1}{2}(-x-1)^2-\dfrac{1}{2}\\&=\dfrac{1}{2}\big(-(x+1)\big)^2-\dfrac{1}{2}\\&=\dfrac{1}{2}(x+1)^2-\dfrac{1}{2}\end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ the vertex is $\left(-1,-\dfrac{1}{2}\right)$.

The $x$-intercepts are where $g(x)=0$:
$$\begin{aligned}0&=\dfrac{1}{2}(x+1)^2-\dfrac{1}{2}\\ \dfrac{1}{2}&=\dfrac{1}{2}(x+1)^2\\1&=(x+1)^2\\ \pm 1&=x+1\\x&=0\text{ or }x=-2\end{aligned}$$','1: vertex; 1: intercepts',163,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correct vertex or intercepts, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "vertex"], [1, "intercepts"]], "top_criterion_original": "intercepts", "source_original": "$f(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(((-x+2)-3)^2-1\\right)$ ... When $f(x)=0$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the transformed function was labelled $f(x)$ (and \"when $f(x)=0$\"); it is $g(x)$. Working unchanged."}');
