$$\begin{aligned}\dot{x}&=\int\ddot{x}\,dt\\&=\dfrac{12e^{-2t}}{-2}+\dfrac{e^{-t}}{-1}+C\\&=-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+C\end{aligned}$$
At $t=0$, $\dot{x}=-6$:
$$\begin{aligned}-6&=-6-1+C\\C&=1\end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\ \dot{x}=-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+1$$
Integrating the velocity:
$$\begin{aligned}x&=\int\dot{x}\,dt\\&=\dfrac{-6e^{-2t}}{-2}-\dfrac{e^{-t}}{-1}+t+C_2\\&=3e^{-2t}+e^{-t}+t+C_2\end{aligned}$$
At $t=0$, $x=8$:
$$\begin{aligned}8&=3+1+0+C_2\\C_2&=4\end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore\ x=3e^{-2t}+e^{-t}+t+4$$','1: $\dot{x}=-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+C$; 1: $x=3e^{-2t}+e^{-t}+t+C_2$; 1: $C_2=4$',165,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds $x=3e^{-2t}+e^{-t}+t+C_2$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds $\\dot{x}=-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+C$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "$\\dot{x}=-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+C$"], [1, "$x=3e^{-2t}+e^{-t}+t+C_2$"], [1, "$C_2=4$"]], "top_criterion_original": "$C_2=4$"}');
$$-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+1=0$$
Multiplying by $e^{2t}$ gives a quadratic in $e^t$:
$$\begin{aligned}-6-e^t+e^{2t}&=0\\(e^t)^2-e^t-6&=0\\(e^t+2)(e^t-3)&=0\end{aligned}$$
So $e^t=-2$ or $e^t=3$.

$e^t>0$, so $e^t=-2$ has no solution.
$$\begin{aligned}e^t&=3\\t&=\ln3\end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ the particle is at rest after $t=\ln3$ seconds.','1: $-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+1=0$; 1: $(e^t+2)(e^t-3)=0$; 1: $t=\ln3$ (rejecting $e^t=-2$)',165,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds $(e^t+2)(e^t-3)=0$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Writes $-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+1=0$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "$-6e^{-2t}-e^{-t}+1=0$"], [1, "$(e^t+2)(e^t-3)=0$"], [1, "$t=\\ln3$ (rejecting $e^t=-2$)"]], "top_criterion_original": "$t=\\ln3$ (rejecting $e^t=-2$)", "marker_note": "Full marks need $t=\\ln3$ with $e^t=-2$ rejected."}');
