$$A_{240}=P(1.005)^{240}-7000\left[1.005^{239}+1.005^{238}+\ldots+1\right]$$
The bracket is a geometric series with $a=1$, $r=1.005$, 240 terms, using $S_n=\dfrac{a(r^n-1)}{r-1}$:
$$\begin{aligned}A_{240}&=P(1.005)^{240}-7000\left[\dfrac{1.005^{240}-1}{0.005}\right]\\ &=P(1.005)^{240}-1400000\left(1.005^{240}-1\right)\end{aligned}$$
The account is empty after 240 withdrawals (20 years), so $A_{240}=0$:
$$\begin{aligned}0&=P(1.005)^{240}-1400000\left(1.005^{240}-1\right)\\ P(1.005)^{240}&=1400000\left(1.005^{240}-1\right)\\ P&=\dfrac{1400000\left(1.005^{240}-1\right)}{1.005^{240}}\\ P&=\$977\,065.40\end{aligned}$$','1: sums the geometric series; 1: $P=\$977\,065.40$',166,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Sums the geometric series, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "sums the geometric series"], [1, "$P=\\$977\\,065.40$"]], "top_criterion_original": "$P=\\$977\\,065.40$", "source_original": "$$A_{240}=P(1.005)^{240}-7000\\left[\\dfrac{1.005^{240}-1}{1.005}\\right]$$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the GP sum denominator was written $1.005$; it is $1.005-1=0.005$ (the next line, $1400000$, and the answer are unchanged)."}');

