In right-angled triangle $MBC$ (angle of elevation $5^\circ$, $MB=105$):
$$\begin{aligned}\tan 5^\circ&=\dfrac{105}{BC}\\ BC&=\dfrac{105}{\tan 5^\circ}\\ &=105\cot 5^\circ\end{aligned}$$
In right-angled triangle $MBS$ (angle of elevation $7^\circ$):
$$\begin{aligned}\tan 7^\circ&=\dfrac{105}{BS}\\ BS&=\dfrac{105}{\tan 7^\circ}\\ &=105\cot 7^\circ\end{aligned}$$
Using the cosine rule in triangle $CBS$ with $\angle CBS=52^\circ$:
$$\begin{aligned}CS^2&=(105\cot 5^\circ)^2+(105\cot 7^\circ)^2-2(105\cot 5^\circ)(105\cot 7^\circ)\cos 52^\circ\\ &=\dfrac{105^2}{\tan^2 5^\circ}+\dfrac{105^2}{\tan^2 7^\circ}-\dfrac{2\times 105^2\cos 52^\circ}{\tan 5^\circ\tan 7^\circ}\\ &\approx 907\,933.4963\ldots\\ CS&=952.8554\ldots\\ &\approx 953\text{ m (nearest metre)}\end{aligned}$$','1: finds $BC$ or $BS$ (either); 1: correct cosine rule; 1: 953 m',166,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correct cosine rule, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds $BC$ or $BS$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "finds $BC$ or $BS$ (either)"], [1, "correct cosine rule"], [1, "953 m"]], "top_criterion_original": "953 m"}');
