$$\begin{aligned}A_{\text{curve}}&=\int_0^4 p^x\,dx\\ &=\left[\dfrac{p^x}{\ln p}\right]_0^4\\ &=\dfrac{p^4}{\ln p}-\dfrac{p^0}{\ln p}\\ &=\dfrac{p^4-1}{\ln p}\end{aligned}$$
From the diagram, the rectangles lie under the curve, so $A_{\text{rect}}<A_{\text{curve}}$:
$$\begin{aligned}\dfrac{p^4-1}{p-1}&<\dfrac{p^4-1}{\ln p}\\ \dfrac{1}{p-1}&<\dfrac{1}{\ln p}\\ \ln p&<p-1\quad\text{as }p>1\end{aligned}$$','1: $\left[\dfrac{p^x}{\ln p}\right]_0^4$; 1: $\dfrac{p^4-1}{p-1}<\dfrac{p^4-1}{\ln p}$; 1: $\ln p<p-1$',166,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Obtains $\\dfrac{p^4-1}{p-1}<\\dfrac{p^4-1}{\\ln p}$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds $\\left[\\dfrac{p^x}{\\ln p}\\right]_0^4$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "$\\left[\\dfrac{p^x}{\\ln p}\\right]_0^4$"], [1, "$\\dfrac{p^4-1}{p-1}<\\dfrac{p^4-1}{\\ln p}$"], [1, "$\\ln p<p-1$"]], "top_criterion_original": "$\\ln p<p-1$"}');
