$$\begin{aligned} A &= \int_0^{10}\left(-\dfrac{x^2}{25}+\dfrac{x}{5}-4-\left(-(2x+16)^{\frac{1}{2}}\right)\right)dx \\ &= \int_0^{10}\left(-\dfrac{x^2}{25}+\dfrac{x}{5}-4\right)dx+\dfrac{1}{2}\int_0^{10}2(2x+16)^{\frac{1}{2}}\,dx \\ &= \left[-\dfrac{x^3}{75}+\dfrac{x^2}{10}-4x\right]_0^{10}+\dfrac{1}{2}\left[\dfrac{2(2x+16)^{\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\right]_0^{10} \\ &= \left(-\dfrac{10^3}{75}+\dfrac{10^2}{10}-4(10)-0\right)+\left(\dfrac{(2(10)+16)^{\frac{3}{2}}}{3}-\dfrac{(2(0)+16)^{\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\right) \\ &= -\dfrac{130}{3}+\dfrac{152}{3} \\ &= \dfrac{22}{3}\text{ units}^2 \end{aligned}$$','4: Correct answer; 3: Correct substitution of the limits, or equivalent merit; 2: Correct primitives, or equivalent merit; 1: Correct integral expression for the area, or equivalent merit',309,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Correct substitution of the limits, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Correct primitives, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correct integral expression for the area, or equivalent merit"]]','{}');
$$\begin{aligned}u&=10e^{-x} & v&=1-x\\ u''&=-10e^{-x} & v''&=-1\end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} f''(x) &= u''v+uv'' \\ &= -10e^{-x}(1-x)-10e^{-x} \\ &= -10e^{-x}(1-x+1) \\ &= -10e^{-x}(2-x) \end{aligned}$$
Stationary points when $f''(x)=0$.

$-10e^{-x}=0$ has no solutions, so $2-x=0$:
$$x=2$$
Using the product rule on $f''(x)=-10e^{-x}(2-x)$, with
$$\begin{aligned}u&=-10e^{-x} & v&=2-x\\ u''&=10e^{-x} & v''&=-1\end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} f''''(x) &= u''v+uv'' \\ &= 10e^{-x}(2-x)+10e^{-x} \\ &= 10e^{-x}(3-x) \end{aligned}$$
Testing the nature at $x=2$:
$$\begin{aligned} f''''(2) &= 10e^{-2}(3-2) \\ &= 1.3\ldots \end{aligned}$$
$f''''(2)>0$, so a local minimum.
$$\begin{aligned} f(2) &= 10e^{-2}(1-2) \\ &= -10e^{-2} \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ $(2,-10e^{-2})$ is a local minimum.','3: Correct answer; 2: Finds $x=2$ and shows it is a local minimum, or equivalent merit; 1: Correct $f''(x)$, or equivalent merit',309,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds $x=2$ and shows it is a local minimum, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correct $f''(x)$, or equivalent merit"]]','{}');
