$R$ is the area under the curve from $x=1$ to $x=4$ plus the triangle under the normal from $P$ to its $x$-intercept.
$$\begin{aligned}y&=\dfrac{16}{x^2}+3x-4\\ &=16x^{-2}+3x-4\\ \dfrac{dy}{dx}&=-32x^{-3}+3\end{aligned}$$
At $P(4,9)$:
$$\begin{aligned}m_{\text{tangent}}&=-32(4)^{-3}+3\\ &=2.5\end{aligned}$$
The normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so $m_1m_2=-1$:
$$\begin{aligned}m_{\text{normal}}&=-\dfrac{1}{2.5}\\ &=-\dfrac{2}{5}\end{aligned}$$
Equation of normal, using $y-y_1=m(x-x_1)$:
$$\begin{aligned}y-9&=-\dfrac{2}{5}(x-4)\\ 5y-45&=-2x+8\\ 2x+5y-53&=0\end{aligned}$$
$x$-intercept ($y=0$):
$$\begin{aligned}2x+5(0)-53&=0\\ 2x&=53\\ x&=26.5\end{aligned}$$
The triangle has base $26.5-4=22.5$ and height 9:
$$\begin{aligned}\text{Area}&=\int_1^4\left(\dfrac{16}{x^2}+3x-4\right)dx+\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\times22.5\times9\right)\\ &=\int_1^4\left(16x^{-2}+3x-4\right)dx+101.25\\ &=\left[\dfrac{16x^{-1}}{-1}+\dfrac{3x^2}{2}-4x\right]_1^4+101.25\\ &=\left[-\dfrac{16}{x}+\dfrac{3x^2}{2}-4x\right]_1^4+101.25\\ &=\left(-\dfrac{16}{4}+\dfrac{3(4)^2}{2}-4(4)\right)-\left(-\dfrac{16}{1}+\dfrac{3(1)^2}{2}-4(1)\right)+101.25\\ &=22.5+101.25\\ &=123.75\text{ u}^2\end{aligned}$$','4: correct solution; 3: correctly forms integration to find area; 2: finds equation of normal and $x$-intercept; 1: differentiates to find gradient of normal',320,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Correctly forms the integral to find the area, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds the equation of the normal and its $x$-intercept, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Differentiates to find the gradient of the normal, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[4, "correct solution"], [3, "correctly forms integration to find area"], [2, "finds equation of normal and $x$-intercept"], [1, "differentiates to find gradient of normal"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct solution"}');

