In right-angled $\triangle TSB$, $\angle STB=42^\circ$:
$$\begin{aligned} \tan 42^\circ&=\dfrac{SB}{50}\\ SB&=50\tan 42^\circ \end{aligned}$$
In right-angled $\triangle TDB$, $\angle DTB=55^\circ$:
$$\begin{aligned} \tan 55^\circ&=\dfrac{BD}{50}\\ BD&=50\tan 55^\circ \end{aligned}$$
Cosine rule in $\triangle SBD$ with $\angle SBD=62^\circ$:
$$\begin{aligned} SD^2&=(50\tan 55^\circ)^2+(50\tan 42^\circ)^2-2(50\tan 55^\circ)(50\tan 42^\circ)\cos 62^\circ\\ &=4107.3439\ldots\\ SD&=\sqrt{4107.3439\ldots}\\ \therefore SD&=64.09 \text{ m} \end{aligned}$$','3: Correct answer; 2: Correct cosine rule set up, or equivalent merit; 1: Finds both $SB$ and $BD$, or equivalent merit',323,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correct cosine rule set up, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds both $SB$ and $BD$, or equivalent merit"]]','{}');
