At $A$, $AC$ makes $30^\circ$ with due south (alternate angles, $BC$ parallel to the north line), so
$$\angle BAC=294^\circ-180^\circ-30^\circ=84^\circ$$
$\angle CBA=180^\circ-84^\circ-30^\circ=66^\circ$ (angle sum of $\triangle ABC$)

Using the sine rule, with $AB=18$ opposite the $30^\circ$ angle:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{AC}{\sin66^\circ}&=\dfrac{18}{\sin30^\circ}\\ AC&=\dfrac{18}{\sin30^\circ}\times\sin66^\circ\\ &=32.88763648 \end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{BC}{\sin84^\circ}&=\dfrac{18}{\sin30^\circ}\\ BC&=\dfrac{18}{\sin30^\circ}\times\sin84^\circ\\ &=35.80278823 \end{aligned}$$
Perimeter of the triangle:
$$\begin{aligned} P&=18+32.88763648+35.80278823\\ &=86.6904\ldots\\ &\approx86.7 \text{ (3 sig. fig.)} \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ The total length of the race is 86.7 km, correct to three significant figures.','5: Provides correct solution; 4: Correctly finds perimeter of triangle with incorrect rounding, or equivalent merit; 3: Uses sine rule to find either side $AC$ or $BC$, or equivalent merit; 2: Correctly finds all angles inside the triangle, or equivalent merit; 1: Correctly finds $\angle BAC$, or equivalent merit',641,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[5, "Correct answer"], [4, "Correctly finds perimeter of triangle with incorrect rounding, or equivalent merit"], [3, "Uses sine rule to find either side $AC$ or $BC$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Correctly finds all angles inside the triangle, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly finds $\\angle BAC$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[5, "Provides correct solution"], [4, "Correctly finds perimeter of triangle with incorrect rounding, or equivalent merit"], [3, "Uses sine rule to find either side $AC$ or $BC$, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Correctly finds all angles inside the triangle, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly finds $\\angle BAC$, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution", "source_original": "\\angle BAC=\\angle BCA=30^\\circ (alternate angles)", "corrected": "Corrected from source: only angle BCA is 30 degrees; angle BAC = 294 - 180 - 30 = 84 degrees, the value the working then uses."}');
$$\begin{aligned} u&=\ln(x-1) & v&=x-1\\ u''&=\dfrac{1}{x-1} & v''&=1 \end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} y''&=\dfrac{\frac{1}{x-1}\times(x-1)-\ln(x-1)}{(x-1)^2}\\ &=\dfrac{1-\ln(x-1)}{(x-1)^2} \end{aligned}$$
At $x=2$, the gradient of the tangent is
$$\dfrac{1-\ln(2-1)}{(2-1)^2}=1$$
Hence the gradient of the normal is $-1$ (negative reciprocal).

Using the point-gradient formula for the normal through $(2,0)$:
$$\begin{aligned} y-0&=-1(x-2)\\ \therefore\ y&=2-x \end{aligned}$$','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Finds the equation of the tangent instead of the normal, or finds the gradient of the normal but not the equation of the normal, or equivalent merit; 1: Correctly applies quotient rule, or equivalent merit',641,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds the equation of the tangent instead of the normal, or finds the gradient of the normal but not the equation of the normal, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly applies quotient rule, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Provides correct solution"], [2, "Finds the equation of the tangent instead of the normal, or finds the gradient of the normal but not the equation of the normal, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly applies quotient rule, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');

The centre measurement of the lake is
$$450-70-80=300$$
Using the trapezoidal rule with 2 strips along the 700 m length, $h=\dfrac{700}{2}=350$:
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area of lake}&\approx\dfrac{350}{2}(80+2\times300+100)\\ &=136\,500 \text{ m}^2 \end{aligned}$$
$$\text{Area of rectangle}=700\times450=315\,000 \text{ m}^2$$
$$\begin{aligned} P(\text{success})&=\dfrac{\text{Area of lake}}{\text{Area of rectangle}}\\ &=\dfrac{136\,500}{315\,000}\\ &=\dfrac{13}{30} \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ The probability that the monitoring system will drop onto the lake is $\dfrac{13}{30}$, or about $43.3\%$.','4: Provides correct solution; 3: Correctly finds the area of the lake and the rectangle, or equivalent merit; 2: Correctly finds the area of the lake using the Trapezoidal rule, or equivalent merit; 1: Recognises that the probability of success is found by dividing the area of the lake by the area of the rectangle, or equivalent merit',641,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Correctly finds the area of the lake and the rectangle, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Correctly finds the area of the lake using the Trapezoidal rule, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Recognises that the probability of success is found by dividing the area of the lake by the area of the rectangle, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[4, "Provides correct solution"], [3, "Correctly finds the area of the lake and the rectangle, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Correctly finds the area of the lake using the Trapezoidal rule, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Recognises that the probability of success is found by dividing the area of the lake by the area of the rectangle, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');

