The labelled weight is 2 kg:
$$z=\dfrac{2-2.05}{0.05}=-1$$
By the empirical rule, $34\%$ of bags lie between $z=-1$ and the mean, so
$$\begin{aligned} P(z<-1)&=50\%-34\%\\ &=16\% \end{aligned}$$
$$16\%\times 2000=320$$
$\therefore$ 320 bags contain less than the labelled weight.','2: Provides correct solution; 1: Provides correct percentage OEM',335,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Provides correct percentage, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Provides correct solution"], [1, "Provides correct percentage OEM"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');

