$$\begin{aligned} \int_0^1\sqrt{1-x^2}\,dx&=\text{area of quadrant}\\ &=\dfrac{1}{4}\times\pi\times 1^2\\ &=\dfrac{\pi}{4} \end{aligned}$$
Using the estimate from part (a):
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{\pi}{4}&\approx 0.748927\ldots\\ \pi&\approx 2.99570\ldots\\ &\approx 2.996 \end{aligned}$$','2: Provides correct solution; 1: Provides correct exact value of the definite integral, or equivalent merit',335,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Provides correct exact value of the definite integral, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Provides correct solution"], [1, "Provides correct exact value of the definite integral, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
