$$\begin{aligned} \int_0^{\frac{\pi}{3}}\tan^2 x\left(\dfrac{\operatorname{cosec}x}{\operatorname{cosec}x-\sin x}\right)dx&=\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{3}}\tan^2 x\sec^2 x\,dx\\ &=\left[\dfrac{1}{3}\tan^3 x\right]_0^{\frac{\pi}{3}}\\ &=\dfrac{1}{3}\left[\tan^3\left(\dfrac{\pi}{3}\right)-\tan^3(0)\right]\\ &=\dfrac{1}{3}\left[\left(\sqrt{3}\right)^3-0\right]\\ &=\dfrac{1}{3}\left(3\sqrt{3}\right)\\ &=\sqrt{3} \end{aligned}$$','2: Provides correct solution; 1: Recognises the integral is of the form $\displaystyle\int f''(x)\big[f(x)\big]^n\,dx$, or equivalent merit',335,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Recognises the integral is of the form $\\displaystyle\\int f''(x)\\big[f(x)\\big]^n\\,dx$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Provides correct solution"], [1, "Recognises the integral is of the form $\\displaystyle\\int f''(x)\\big[f(x)\\big]^n\\,dx$, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
