The wire forms two radii and the arc $l=r\theta$:
$$\begin{aligned} L&=2r+r\theta\\ r\theta&=L-2r\\ \theta&=\dfrac{L-2r}{r} \end{aligned}$$','2: Provides correct solution; 1: Provides an expression for $L$ in terms of $r$ and $\theta$, or equivalent merit',335,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Provides an expression for $L$ in terms of $r$ and $\\theta$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"source_original": "last line written as \\theta = \\dfrac{L-2r}{\\theta}", "corrected": "Corrected from source: denominator of the last line is r, not theta.", "criteria_original": [[2, "Provides correct solution"], [1, "Provides an expression for $L$ in terms of $r$ and $\\theta$, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
$$\begin{aligned} A&=\dfrac{1}{2}r^2\theta\\ &=\dfrac{1}{2}r^2\left(\dfrac{L-2r}{r}\right)\\ &=\dfrac{Lr}{2}-r^2 \end{aligned}$$
For maximum area, need
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{dA}{dr}&=0\\ \dfrac{d^2A}{dr^2}&<0 \end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{dA}{dr}&=\dfrac{L}{2}-2r\\ 0&=\dfrac{L}{2}-2r\\ 2r&=\dfrac{L}{2}\\ r&=\dfrac{L}{4} \end{aligned}$$
$$\dfrac{d^2A}{dr^2}=-2<0$$
Thus area is maximised when $r=\dfrac{L}{4}$.','3: Provides correct solution; 2: Correctly shows there is a stationary point at $r=\dfrac{L}{4}$ but fails to show it is a maximum, or equivalent merit; 1: Provides a correct expression for $A$ in terms of $r$ and $L$, or equivalent merit',335,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correctly shows there is a stationary point at $r=\\dfrac{L}{4}$ but fails to show it is a maximum, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Provides a correct expression for $A$ in terms of $r$ and $L$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "Provides correct solution"], [2, "Correctly shows there is a stationary point at $r=\\dfrac{L}{4}$ but fails to show it is a maximum, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Provides a correct expression for $A$ in terms of $r$ and $L$, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Provides correct solution"}');
