$$\begin{aligned} \int_{-3}^{8} f(x)\,dx &= \int_{-3}^{2} f(x)\,dx+\int_{2}^{8} f(x)\,dx \\ A &= \int_{-3}^{2} f(x)\,dx+B \\ \int_{-3}^{2} f(x)\,dx &= A-B \end{aligned}$$

Reversing the limits,

$$\int_{2}^{-3} f(x)\,dx=-(A-B)=B-A$$

Then

$$\begin{aligned} \int_{2}^{-3}\left(f(x)+2x\right)dx &= \int_{2}^{-3} f(x)\,dx+\int_{2}^{-3} 2x\,dx \\ &= B-A+\left[x^2\right]_{2}^{-3} \\ &= B-A+9-4 \\ &= B-A+5 \end{aligned}$$','1: B',339,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "B"]], "top_criterion_original": "B"}');

