When the coin lands tails, the number recorded is the difference of the dice. A win needs a difference less than $4$, which occurs in $30$ of the $36$ outcomes.

$$\begin{aligned} P(\text{win}\mid T) &= \dfrac{30}{36} \\ &= \dfrac{5}{6} \end{aligned}$$','1: correct answer',347,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[1, "Correct answer"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');

When the coin lands heads, a win needs a sum less than $4$, which occurs in $3$ of the $36$ outcomes, so $P(\text{win}\mid H)=\dfrac{3}{36}$.

Heads and tails are equally likely:

$$\begin{aligned} P(\text{win}) &= \dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{30}{36}\right)+\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{3}{36}\right) \\ &= \dfrac{11}{24} \end{aligned}$$','2: correct answer; 1: progress beyond part (a) such as finding $P(\text{win}\mid H)=\frac{3}{36}$; 0: insufficient progress',347,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Progresses beyond part (a), such as finding $P(\\text{win}\\mid H)=\\dfrac{3}{36}$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "correct answer"], [1, "progress beyond part (a) such as finding $P(\\text{win}\\mid H)=\\dfrac{3}{36}$"], [0, "insufficient progress"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct answer"}');

