$$V=\dfrac{x}{2}\left(1+\dfrac{2x}{3}\right)y \qquad (1)$$

The perimeter is $27$ m:

$$\begin{aligned} 2x+2y &= 27 \\ y &= \dfrac{27}{2}-x \qquad (2) \end{aligned}$$

Substitute (2) into (1):

$$\begin{aligned} V &= \dfrac{x}{2}\left(1+\dfrac{2x}{3}\right)\left(\dfrac{27}{2}-x\right) \\ &= \dfrac{x}{2}\left(\dfrac{27}{2}-x+9x-\dfrac{2x^2}{3}\right) \\ &= \dfrac{x}{2}\left(\dfrac{27}{2}+8x-\dfrac{2x^2}{3}\right) \\ V(x) &= -\dfrac{x^3}{3}+4x^2+\dfrac{27}{4}x \end{aligned}$$','1: correctly substitutes eq. 2 into eq. 1 or equivalent; 1: sufficiently shows result',347,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correctly substitutes equation (2) into equation (1), or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correctly substitutes eq. 2 into eq. 1 or equivalent"], [1, "sufficiently shows result"]], "top_criterion_original": "correctly substitutes eq. 2 into eq. 1 or equivalent"}');

$$V''(x)=-x^2+8x+\dfrac{27}{4}$$

$$\begin{aligned} 0 &= x^2-8x-\dfrac{27}{4} \\ x &= \dfrac{8\pm\sqrt{64-4(1)\left(-\frac{27}{4}\right)}}{2} \\ &= \dfrac{8\pm\sqrt{91}}{2} \\ &\approx 8.7697 \text{ or } -0.77 \end{aligned}$$

Length is positive, so ignore the negative value.

$$\begin{aligned} V(8.7697) &= -\dfrac{(8.7697)^3}{3}+4(8.7697)^2+\dfrac{27}{4}(8.7697) \\ &= 142\text{ m}^3 \text{ (3 significant figures)} \end{aligned}$$','1: correctly differentiates $V(x)$; 1: correctly solves the quadratic; 1: correctly uses original formula to find volume',347,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correctly solves the quadratic, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly differentiates $V(x)$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correctly differentiates $V(x)$"], [1, "correctly solves the quadratic"], [1, "correctly uses original formula to find volume"]], "top_criterion_original": "correctly differentiates $V(x)$", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the handwritten substitution omitted the minus sign on the $\\frac{x^3}{3}$ term; it should read $-\\frac{x^3}{3}$ (final value 142 unchanged).", "source_original": "handwritten working omits the minus sign on the $\\frac{x^3}{3}$ term when substituting into $V$; final value 142 is correct for $V(x)$ as given; kept as printed"}');

$$V''''(8.7697)\approx -9.5$$

$$\begin{aligned} V''(8.7697) &= 0 &&\text{stationary point} \\ V''''(8.7697) &< 0 &&\text{concave down} \end{aligned}$$

So the stationary point is a local maximum.

The domain is $0<x<13.5$ because the perimeter is $27$ m, and $V(0)=V(13.5)=0$.

