Using the quotient rule, $\dfrac{d}{d\theta}\left(\dfrac{u}{v}\right)=\dfrac{u''v-uv''}{v^2}$, with
$$\begin{aligned} u&=100 & v&=5-4\sin^2\theta \\ u''&=0 & v''&=-8\sin\theta\cos\theta \end{aligned}$$
$$\dfrac{dS}{d\theta}=\dfrac{-100\left(-8\sin\theta\cos\theta\right)}{\left(5-4\sin^2\theta\right)^2}$$
$\dfrac{dS}{d\theta}=0$ when $\sin\theta\cos\theta=0$. In the domain $\sin\theta\ne0$, so $\cos\theta=0$:
$$\theta=\dfrac{\pi}{2} \text{ or } \dfrac{3\pi}{2}$$
Test the values of $S$ just either side of each:
$$\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\theta&\dfrac{\pi}{2}-0.01&\dfrac{\pi}{2}&\dfrac{\pi}{2}+0.01\\\hline S&99.96&100&99.96\end{array}$$
$$\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\theta&\dfrac{3\pi}{2}-0.01&\dfrac{3\pi}{2}&\dfrac{3\pi}{2}+0.01\\\hline S&99.96&100&99.96\end{array}$$
$\therefore$ the sum is greatest at $\theta=\dfrac{\pi}{2}$ or $\theta=\dfrac{3\pi}{2}$.','1: correct working; 1: correct answer',361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Correct working, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correct working"], [1, "correct answer"]], "checked_source_ok": "dS/dtheta=800 sin cos/(5-4sin^2)^2 verified; max S=100 at theta=pi/2, 3pi/2"}');
$$\begin{aligned} A&=\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}\sqrt{2}\sin 2x\,dx+\int_{\frac{\pi}{4}}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}2\cos x\,dx \\ &=\left[-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\cos 2x\right]_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}+\Big[2\sin x\Big]_{\frac{\pi}{4}}^{\frac{\pi}{2}} \\ &=\left[-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\times0-\left(-\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\right)\right]+\left[2\times1-2\times\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right] \\ &=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}}+2-\sqrt{2} \\ &=\dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{2}+\dfrac{4}{2}-\dfrac{2\sqrt{2}}{2} \\ &=\dfrac{4-\sqrt{2}}{2} \end{aligned}$$','3: provide correct solutions; 2: provide correct working and wrong answer; 1: correct answer',361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Provides correct working and a wrong answer, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correct answer, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "provide correct solutions"], [2, "provide correct working and wrong answer"], [1, "correct answer"]], "top_criterion_original": "provide correct solutions"}');
$$\begin{aligned} P(N=0)&=\dfrac{2}{3} \\ P(N=1)&=\dfrac{2}{9} \\ P(N\ge2)&=\dfrac{1}{9} \end{aligned}$$
Solution 1:

\exfigure{361_q34_s1}
$$P(\text{at least one month with zero claims})=1-\dfrac{1}{3}\times\dfrac{1}{3}=\dfrac{8}{9}$$
More than one claim in total, given a zero month, means one month has zero claims and the other has $2$ or more:
$$\begin{aligned} P(N>1\mid\text{at least one zero month})&=\dfrac{\frac{1}{9}\times\frac{2}{3}+\frac{2}{3}\times\frac{1}{9}}{\frac{2}{3}\times\frac{1}{3}+\frac{1}{3}\times\frac{2}{3}+\frac{2}{3}\times\frac{2}{3}} \\ &=\dfrac{\frac{4}{27}}{\frac{8}{9}} \\ &=\dfrac{1}{6} \end{aligned}$$
Solution 2:
$$\begin{aligned} P&=1-\dfrac{P(0)P(0)+P(0)P(1)+P(1)P(0)}{P(0,0)+P(0,n)+P(n,0)} \\ &=1-\dfrac{\frac{2}{3}\times\frac{2}{3}+\frac{2}{3}\times\frac{2}{9}+\frac{2}{9}\times\frac{2}{3}}{\frac{8}{9}} \\ &=1-\dfrac{\frac{4}{9}+\frac{8}{27}}{\frac{8}{9}} \\ &=1-\dfrac{5}{6} \\ &=\dfrac{1}{6} \end{aligned}$$','1: correctly recognise the sum of three combination events on the numerator; 1: correct working; 1: correct answer',361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Correct working, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Correctly recognises the sum of three combination events in the numerator, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "correctly recognise the sum of three combination events on the numerator"], [1, "correct working"], [1, "correct answer"]], "checked_source_ok": "verified: (4/27)/(8/9)=1/6 and 1-(20/27)/(8/9)=1/6; both clean restatements match the source answer"}');
$$\begin{aligned} A_1&=Q\times1.035-8000 \\ A_2&=A_1\times1.035-8000 \\ &=\left(Q\times1.035-8000\right)1.035-8000 \\ &=Q\times1.035^2-8000\times1.035-8000 \\ A_3&=A_2\times1.035-8000 \\ &=Q\times1.035^3-8000\times1.035^2-8000\times1.035-8000 \\ &=Q\times1.035^3-8000\left(1.035^2+1.035+1\right) \end{aligned}$$
Continuing the pattern,
$$A_n=Q\times1.035^n-8000\left(1+1.035+\cdots+1.035^{n-1}\right)$$
The minimum value of $Q$ leaves nothing after $n$ withdrawals, $A_n=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} Q\times1.035^n&=8000\left(1+1.035+1.035^2+1.035^3+\cdots+1.035^{n-1}\right) \\ Q&=\dfrac{8000}{1.035^n}+\dfrac{8000}{1.035^{n-1}}+\dfrac{8000}{1.035^{n-2}}+\cdots+\dfrac{8000}{1.035} \\ &=\dfrac{8000}{1.035}+\dfrac{8000}{1.035^2}+\cdots+\dfrac{8000}{1.035^n} \end{aligned}$$','3: provide correct solutions; 2: find the correct expression for $A_n$; 1: write the correct expression for $A_1$, $A_2$ or $A_3$',361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds the correct expression for $A_n$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Writes the correct expression for $A_1$, $A_2$ or $A_3$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[3, "provide correct solutions"], [2, "find the correct expression for $A_n$"], [1, "write the correct expression for $A_1$, $A_2$ or $A_3$"]], "top_criterion_original": "provide correct solutions"}');
$$\begin{aligned} a&=\dfrac{8000}{1.035} \\ r&=\dfrac{1}{1.035} \end{aligned}$$
Withdrawing indefinitely means $n\to\infty$, so the minimum value is the limiting sum (as $|r|<1$):
$$\begin{aligned} Q&=\dfrac{a}{1-r} \\ &=\dfrac{\frac{8000}{1.035}}{1-\frac{1}{1.035}} \\ &=\$228\,571.43 \\ &\approx\$228\,571 \text{ (nearest dollar)} \end{aligned}$$
Alternative solution: the yearly interest must cover the withdrawal, so
$$\begin{aligned} Q\times3.5\%&=8000 \\ Q&=\dfrac{8000}{3.5\%} \\ &=\$228\,571.43 \end{aligned}$$','2: provide correct solutions; 1: using the correct limiting sum expression to find the minimum value',361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Uses the correct limiting sum expression to find the minimum value, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "provide correct solutions"], [1, "using the correct limiting sum expression to find the minimum value"]], "top_criterion_original": "provide correct solutions", "corrected": "Corrected from source: the question asks for the nearest dollar, so the answer is $\\$228\\,571$; the guideline stopped at $\\$228\\,571.43$.", "source_original": "Minimum value $=\\dfrac{\\frac{8000}{1.035}}{1-\\frac{1}{1.035}}=\\$228\\,571.43$"}');
$$\text{Arc } AB=12-2\sqrt{3}-3x$$
Arc length is $x\theta$:
$$\begin{aligned} x\theta&=12-2\sqrt{3}-3x \\ \theta&=\dfrac{12}{x}-\dfrac{2\sqrt{3}}{x}-3 \end{aligned}$$
Triangle $BCO$ is equilateral, so $\angle BOC=\dfrac{\pi}{3}$:
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area } \triangle OBC&=\dfrac{1}{2}\times x^2\times\sin\left(\dfrac{\pi}{3}\right) \\ &=\dfrac{1}{2}\times x^2\times\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \\ &=\dfrac{\sqrt{3}x^2}{4} \end{aligned}$$
$$\text{Area of sector}=\dfrac{1}{2}x^2\theta=\dfrac{x^2}{2}\theta$$
Area of the precinct is the area of the triangle plus the area of the sector:
$$\begin{aligned} A&=\dfrac{\sqrt{3}x^2}{4}+\dfrac{x^2}{2}\left(\dfrac{12}{x}-\dfrac{2\sqrt{3}}{x}-3\right) \\ &=\dfrac{\sqrt{3}x^2}{4}+6x-\sqrt{3}x-\dfrac{3x^2}{2} \\ &=\dfrac{(\sqrt{3}-6)x^2}{4}+(6-\sqrt{3})x \end{aligned}$$
$$\dfrac{dA}{dx}=\dfrac{(\sqrt{3}-6)x}{2}+(6-\sqrt{3})$$
For a stationary point, $\dfrac{dA}{dx}=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{(\sqrt{3}-6)x}{2}+(6-\sqrt{3})&=0 \\ x&=\dfrac{-2(6-\sqrt{3})}{\sqrt{3}-6} \\ &=\dfrac{2(\sqrt{3}-6)}{\sqrt{3}-6} \\ &=2 \end{aligned}$$
Since $\dfrac{d^2A}{dx^2}=\dfrac{\sqrt{3}-6}{2}<0$, $x=2$ gives a maximum.
$$\begin{aligned} A&=\dfrac{4(\sqrt{3}-6)}{4}+2(6-\sqrt{3}) \\ &=6-\sqrt{3} \text{ km}^2 \end{aligned}$$','5: provide correct solutions; 4: find the expression of $\dfrac{dA}{dx}$, or equivalent merit; 3: find the correct expression of the total area of the precinct; 2: find the correct expression for the area of the triangle or the area of the sector in terms of $x$ or $\theta$; 1: find the correct expression of $\theta$ in terms of $x$, or (criterion cut off at foot of page)',361,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[5, "Correct answer"], [4, "Finds the expression for $\\dfrac{dA}{dx}$, or equivalent merit"], [3, "Finds the correct expression for the total area of the precinct, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds the correct expression for the area of the triangle or the area of the sector in terms of $x$ or $\\theta$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the correct expression for $\\theta$ in terms of $x$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[5, "provide correct solutions"], [4, "find the expression of $\\dfrac{dA}{dx}$, or equivalent merit"], [3, "find the correct expression of the total area of the precinct"], [2, "find the correct expression for the area of the triangle or the area of the sector in terms of $x$ or $\\theta$"], [1, "find the correct expression of $\\theta$ in terms of $x$, or (criterion cut off at foot of page)"]], "top_criterion_original": "provide correct solutions", "criteria_inferred": "Cut-off end of 1-mark row inferred as ''or equivalent merit'' from the same rubric''s 4-mark row and 2024 Gosford AT4 Q32b, 2025 Normanhurst AT4 Q29b, 2025 NSGHS AT4 Q29c, 2025 Killara AT4 Q31c"}');
