$$\begin{aligned} \text{Total area}&=\dfrac{\pi x^2}{4\pi^2}+\left(\dfrac{100-x}{4}\right)^2 \\ &=\dfrac{x^2}{4\pi}+\dfrac{(100-x)^2}{16} \end{aligned}$$','2: Correct derivation; 1: Finds the area of the circle or the area of the square, or equivalent merit',1601,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds the area of the circle or the area of the square, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "Correct derivation"], [1, "Finds the area of the circle or the area of the square, or equivalent merit"]], "top_criterion_original": "Correct derivation"}');
