Alternatively, solve algebraically in two cases.

Case 1, $x-1\ge0$, so $|x-1|=x-1$:
$$\begin{aligned} x-1&=2x+4 \\ -x&=5 \\ x&=-5 \end{aligned}$$
This does not satisfy $x\ge1$, so reject.

Case 2, $x-1<0$, so $|x-1|=-(x-1)=1-x$:
$$\begin{aligned} 1-x&=2x+4 \\ -3x&=3 \\ x&=-1 \end{aligned}$$
Check: $-1<1$, so this satisfies $x-1<0$.
$$\therefore x=-1$$','2: x = -1 with the line y = 2x + 4 sketched, or both cases solved with x = -5 rejected; 1: x = -1 found',373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[2, "Correct answer"], [1, "Finds $x=-1$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[2, "x = -1 with the line y = 2x + 4 sketched, or both cases solved with x = -5 rejected"], [1, "x = -1 found"]], "top_criterion_original": "x = -1 with the line y = 2x + 4 sketched, or both cases solved with x = -5 rejected", "corrected": "Corrected from source: in case 2, $|x-1|=-(x-1)=1-x$, so the equation is $1-x=2x+4$ (the guideline wrote $-x-1=2x+4$, which does not give $-3x=3$).", "source_original": "If $x-1<0$: $-x-1=2x+4$, $-3x=3$, $x=-1$"}');
