Using the quotient rule, $\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(\dfrac{u}{v}\right)=\dfrac{u''v-uv''}{v^2}$, with
$$\begin{aligned} u&=2x & v&=x^2+1 \\ u''&=2 & v''&=2x \end{aligned}$$
$$f''''(x)=\dfrac{2(x^2+1)-4x^2}{(x^2+1)^2}$$
Test the nature at $x=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} f''''(0)&=\dfrac{2(0+1)-0}{(0+1)^2} \\ &=2>0 &&\text{concave up} \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore(0,0)$ is a local minimum stationary point.','1: f''(x) = 0 at x = 0; 1: stationary point (0, 0); 1: nature determined',373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[3, "Correct answer"], [2, "Finds the stationary point $(0,0)$, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Shows $f''(x)=0$ at $x=0$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "f''(x) = 0 at x = 0"], [1, "stationary point (0, 0)"], [1, "nature determined"]], "top_criterion_original": "nature determined"}');
