The base is $2x$ by $x$:
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area of base}&=2x\times x=2x^2 \\ \text{Cost of base}&=15\times2x^2=\$30x^2 \end{aligned}$$
The volume is $90\text{ m}^3$:
$$\begin{aligned} V&=h\times2x\times x \\ 90&=2x^2h \\ h&=\dfrac{45}{x^2} \end{aligned}$$
The four sides have total area
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area of sides}&=2\times h\times2x+2\times x\times h \\ &=4xh+2xh \\ &=6xh \\ &=6x\times\dfrac{45}{x^2} \\ &=\dfrac{270}{x} \end{aligned}$$
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Cost of sides}&=20\times\dfrac{270}{x} \\ &=\$\dfrac{5400}{x} \end{aligned}$$
$$\therefore C=30x^2+\dfrac{5400}{x}$$
To minimise the cost, let $\dfrac{dC}{dx}=0$:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{dC}{dx}&=60x-\dfrac{5400}{x^2}=0 \\ 60x&=\dfrac{5400}{x^2} \\ x^3&=90 \\ x&=\sqrt[3]{90} \end{aligned}$$
Check that $x=\sqrt[3]{90}$ is a minimum:
$$\begin{aligned} \dfrac{d^2C}{dx^2}&=60+\dfrac{10800}{x^3} \\ &=60+\dfrac{10800}{90} &&(x^3=90) \\ &=180>0 &&\text{concave up} \end{aligned}$$
$\therefore$ the cost is least when $x=\sqrt[3]{90}$, and the dimensions of the tank are
$$\begin{aligned} \text{length}&=2\sqrt[3]{90} \text{ m} \\ \text{width}&=\sqrt[3]{90} \text{ m} \\ \text{height}&=\dfrac{45}{\left(\sqrt[3]{90}\right)^2}=\dfrac{45}{90^{\frac{2}{3}}} \text{ m} \end{aligned}$$','1: cost of base; 1: cost of sides; 1: total cost shown; 1: x = cube root of 90; 1: minimum verified and dimensions stated',373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[5, "Correct answer"], [4, "Finds $x=\\sqrt[3]{90}$, or equivalent merit"], [3, "Shows the total cost, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Finds the cost of the sides, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the cost of the base, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "cost of base"], [1, "cost of sides"], [1, "total cost shown"], [1, "x = cube root of 90"], [1, "minimum verified and dimensions stated"]], "top_criterion_original": "minimum verified and dimensions stated", "corrected": "Corrected from source: at $x=\\sqrt[3]{90}$, $\\dfrac{d^2C}{dx^2}=60+\\dfrac{10800}{90}=180>0$ (the guideline wrote $2469\\ldots$). The conclusion is unchanged.", "source_original": "$\\dfrac{d^2C}{dx^2}=60+\\dfrac{10800}{x^3}\\Big|_{x=\\sqrt[3]{90}}=2469\\ldots>0$"}');

