Find $P$ where the curves meet:
$$\begin{aligned} 2\tan x-1&=\tan x \\ \tan x&=1 \\ x&=\dfrac{\pi}{4} &&\text{(first solution)} \end{aligned}$$
The area between the curves is
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area}&=\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}\tan x-(2\tan x-1)\,dx \\ &=\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}\left(-\tan x+1\right)dx \\ &=\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}\left(\dfrac{-\sin x}{\cos x}+1\right)dx \end{aligned}$$
Using $\displaystyle\int\dfrac{f''(x)}{f(x)}\,dx=\ln|f(x)|$ with $f(x)=\cos x$:
$$\begin{aligned} \text{Area}&=\Big[\ln(\cos x)+x\Big]_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}} \\ &=\left(\ln\left(\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right)+\dfrac{\pi}{4}\right)-\left(\ln(1)-0\right) \\ &=\ln\left(2^{-\frac{1}{2}}\right)+\dfrac{\pi}{4} \\ &=\dfrac{\pi}{4}-\dfrac{1}{2}\ln2 \end{aligned}$$','1: x-coordinate of P; 1: correct area integral; 1: correct primitive; 1: correct evaluation',373,NULL,'parse-v1',NULL,NULL,'[[4, "Correct answer"], [3, "Correct primitive, or equivalent merit"], [2, "Correct area integral, or equivalent merit"], [1, "Finds the $x$-coordinate of $P$, or equivalent merit"]]','{"criteria_original": [[1, "x-coordinate of P"], [1, "correct area integral"], [1, "correct primitive"], [1, "correct evaluation"]], "top_criterion_original": "correct evaluation"}');
